**65. Vacation of Office of President: The office of the President shall fall vacant in any of the**
following circumstances:
(a) In case he or she tenders resignation in writing to the Vice-President;
(b) In case the motion of impeachment against him or her is adopted under
Article 101;
(c) In case his or her term of the office expires;
(d) In case he or she dies.

**77. Vacation of Office of Prime Minister and Minister: (1) The office of the Prime**
Minister shall fall vacant in any of the following circumstances: -
43
(a) In case he or she tenders resignation in writing to the President;
(b) In case a resolution of confidence is not adopted or a resolution of no
confidence is adopted against him or her pursuant to Article 100;
(c) In case he or she ceases to be a member of the House of
Representatives;
(d) In case he or she dies.
(2) The office of a Minister shall fall vacant in any of the following
circumstances: -
(a) In case he or she tenders resignation in writing to the Prime Minister;
(b) In case the Prime Minister removes him or her from the office;
(c) In case the office of Prime Minister falls vacant pursuant to subclause (a), (b) or (c) of clause (1);
(d) In case he or she dies.
(3) In case the office of Prime Minister falls vacant pursuant to clause (1), the
same Council of Ministers shall continue to act until another Council of Ministers is
constituted.
Provided that in case the Prime Minister dies, the senior-most Minister shall
act as the Prime Minister until a new Prime Minister is appointed.

**131. Vacation of office of Chief Justice or Justice of Supreme Court: The office of the**
Chief Justice or a Justice of the Supreme Court shall fall vacant in any of the
following circumstances:-
(a) In case he or she tenders resignation in writing to the President;
(b) In case he or she attains the age of sixty-five years;
(c) In case a motion of impeachment is adopted against him or her pursuant
to Article 101;
(d) In case the Chief Justice or a Justice of Supreme Court is relieved of his
or her office by the President, in the case of Chief Justice on
recommendation of the Constitutional Council, and in the case of Justice
of Supreme Court, on recommendation of the Judicial Council, on the
ground that he or she is unable to discharge his or her duties because of
physical or mental illness;
(e) In case he or she is punished by a court for a criminal offence involving
moral turpitude;
(f) In case he or she dies.

**169. Vacation of Office of Chief Minister and Minister: (1) The office of the Chief**
Minister shall fall vacant in any of the following circumstances: -
(a) In case he or she tenders resignation in writing to the Chief of
Province;
(b) In case a vote of no confidence is adopted against him or her or a vote
of confidence is not adopted pursuant to Article 188;
(c) In case he or she ceases to be a member of the Provincial Assembly;
(d) In case he or she dies.
(2) The office of a Minister shall fall vacant in any of the following
circumstances: -
(a) In case he or she tenders resignation in writing to the Chief Minister;
(b) In case the Chief Minister removes him or her from the office;
(c) In case the office of the Chief Minister falls vacant pursuant to subclause (a), (b) or (c) of clause (1);
(d) In case he or she dies.
(3) Even though the office of the Chief Minister falls vacant pursuant to clause
(1), the same Council of Ministers shall continue to act until another Provincial
Council of Ministers is constituted.
89
Provided that in case the Chief Minister dies, the senior-most Minister shall
act as the Chief Minister until a new Chief Minister is appointed.

**180. Vacation of Seat of a Member of Provincial Assembly: The seat of a member of the**
Provincial Assembly shall fall vacant in any of the following circumstances:-
(a) In case he or she tenders resignation in writing to the Speaker of
Province;
(b) In case he or she is no longer qualified or ceases to possess the
qualifications referred to in Article 178;
(c) In case the term of the Provincial Assembly expires or it is dissolved;
94
(d) In case he or she is absent in ten consecutive meetings without giving
information to the Provincial Assembly;
(e) In case the political party of which he or she was a member when elected
provides a notification as provided for in the federal law that he or she
has defected from the party;
(f) In case he or she dies.

दफा ४: कम्पनी स्थापनाको लागि निवेदन दिनु पर्ने (Application to be filed for incorporation of company)
रहेको एकल शेयरधनी भएको कम्पनीको स्थापनाको लागि तोकिएको नियमावलीको ढाँचालाई नै संस्थापकले स्वीकार गर्न मञ्जुर गरेमा प्रस्तावित कम्पनीको नियमावली पेश गर्न आवश्यक पर्ने छैन ।

**English Translation:**

4. Application to be filed for incorporation of company: (1) A person wishing to incorporate a company pursuant to Section 3 shall apply to the Office through electronic medium for the approval of the proposed name of the company.
(2) If information is received from the Office that the name of the company has been approved pursuant to sub-section (1), the applicant shall file an application with the Office in the prescribed format by uploading the following documents into the computer system through electronic medium:
(a) The memorandum of association of the proposed company;
(b) The articles of association of the proposed company;
(c) In the case of a public company, a copy of the agreement, if any, entered into between the promoters prior to the incorporation of the company;
(d) In the case of a private company, a copy of the unanimous agreement, if any;

दफा ४: कम्पनी स्थापनाको लागि निवेदन दिनु पर्ने (Application to be filed for incorporation of company)
ompany, a copy of the agreement, if any, entered into between the promoters prior to the incorporation of the company;
(d) In the case of a private company, a copy of the unanimous agreement, if any;
(e) Where the prevailing law requires a prior approval or license from any authority for the registration of a company carrying on any particular type of business or transaction, such approval or license;
(f) Where the promoter is a Nepalese citizen, a certified copy of the citizenship certificate, and where a body corporate is a promoter, the registration certificate of such body, the decision of the board of directors regarding the incorporation of the company and the major instrument relating to the incorporation of such body;
(g) Where a foreign person or company or body is a promoter, the permission obtained under the prevailing law to make investment or carry on business or transaction in Nepal;
(h) Where a foreign person is a promoter, a document proving the citizenship of the country to which he/she belongs;

दफा ४: कम्पनी स्थापनाको लागि निवेदन दिनु पर्ने (Application to be filed for incorporation of company)
he prevailing law to make investment or carry on business or transaction in Nepal;
(h) Where a foreign person is a promoter, a document proving the citizenship of the country to which he/she belongs;
(i) Where a foreign company or body is a promoter, a certified copy of the registration certificate of such company or body and the major instrument relating to its incorporation.
(3) Notwithstanding anything contained in clause (b) of sub-section (2), it shall not be necessary to file the articles of association of the proposed company if the promoter of a company with a single shareholder, where only one person is the promoter, agrees to accept the prescribed format of the articles of association for the incorporation of such company.

दफा ६: कम्पनी दर्ता गर्न इन्कार गर्न सक्ने (Refusal to register company)
ve of the proposed company is contrary to the prevailing law or appears to be improper or undesirable in view of public interest, morality, good conduct, decency, etc., or reflects a criminal intent;
(c) If the name of the proposed company is identical with the name of a company whose registration has been cancelled pursuant to this Act or which has become insolvent under the prevailing law, or so resembles such name as to be likely to create a confusion, and a period of five years has not elapsed since such cancellation of registration or insolvency;
(d) If the requirements for the incorporation of a company under this Act are not fulfilled.
(2) If the Office refuses to register a company in any of the circumstances mentioned in sub-section (1), it shall give a notice thereof, stating the reasons, to the applicant within fifteen days from the date of application for incorporation of the company pursuant to Section 4.
(3) If the Office refuses to register a company pursuant to sub-section (1) or fails to give a notice pursuant to sub-section (2), the person who is not satisfied may file a complaint in the Court within fifteen days.

दफा १८: प्रबन्धपत्र (Memorandum of Association)
्पत्तिको विवरण मूल्याङ्कन गर्दाको आधार उल्लेख गर्नु पर्नेछ ।
(५) प्रबन्धपत्र यस ऐन सँग बाझिएमा बाझिएको हदसम्म स्वतः बदर हुनेछ ।
(६) प्रबन्धपत्रको ढाँचा तोकिए बमोजिम हुनेछ ।

**English Translation:**

18. Memorandum of Association: (1) The memorandum of association of a company shall state the following matters:
(a) The name of the company;
(b) The address of the registered office of the company;
(c) The objectives of the company;
(d) The acts to be carried out to attain the objectives of the company;
(e) The amount of authorized capital of the company, the amount of share capital to be issued by the company for the time being and the amount which the promoters of the company have agreed to pay up;
(f) The types of shares of the company, the rights and powers inherent in such shares, the value of each share and the number of shares of different types;
(g) Any restriction on the purchase or transfer of shares, if any;
(h) The number of shares which the promoters have agreed to take for the time being;
(i) The terms of payment of share amount;
(j) The fact that the liability of the shareholders is limited;
(k) In the case of a private company, the maximum number of shareholders;

दफा १८: प्रबन्धपत्र (Memorandum of Association)
for the time being;
(i) The terms of payment of share amount;
(j) The fact that the liability of the shareholders is limited;
(k) In the case of a private company, the maximum number of shareholders;
(l) Other necessary matters.
(2) In addition to the matters mentioned in sub-section (1), if any of the following matters are to be done or to occur, such matters shall also be mentioned in the memorandum of association:
(a) If a promoter or any other person is to purchase shares or obtain a right in shares for consideration other than cash, such matter;
(b) If the company is to acquire any property in any manner from a promoter or any other person at the time of commencement of its business, such matter;
(c) If the company itself is to bear the expenses incurred in its incorporation, such matter;
(d) If a promoter or any other person is to obtain any special privilege or right from the company, such matter.

दफा २०: नियमावली (Articles of Association)
को बचाउ सम्बन्धमा नियमावलीमा गरिएको कुनै व्यवस्था लगायत यो ऐन तथा प्रबन्धपत्र सँग कुनै व्यवस्था बाझिएमा बाझिएको हदसम्म बदर हुनेछ ।
(४) नियमावलीको ढाँचा तोकिए बमोजिम हुनेछ ।

**English Translation:**

20. Articles of Association: (1) A company shall frame articles of association to attain the objectives set forth in the memorandum of association and to conduct its business in a well-managed manner.
(2) The articles of association shall state the following matters:
(a) The mode of calling the general meeting of the company and the matters relating to the notice of the meeting;
(b) The procedure of the general meeting;
(c) The number of directors, the provision for alternate directors, if any, and the tenure of directors;
(d) Provisions relating to the record of decisions of the general meeting and the board of directors, and the copy and inspection thereof;
(e) The minimum number of shares, if any, to be held by a person to be appointed as a director of the company;
(f) In the case of a public company, the qualification and number of independent directors;

दफा २०: नियमावली (Articles of Association)
The minimum number of shares, if any, to be held by a person to be appointed as a director of the company;
(f) In the case of a public company, the qualification and number of independent directors;
(g) If any professional person other than a shareholder is to be appointed as a director, the number, tenure, qualification and appointment process of such directors;
(h) The powers and duties of the board of directors and the managing director;
(i) The authority of directors and delegation of authority;
(j) The quorum for the meeting of the board of directors, the notice of the meeting and the procedure of the meeting;
(k) Matters relating to lien on shares;
(l) Different classes of shares and the rights, powers and restrictions inherent in such shares;
(m) Provisions relating to calls on shares and forfeiture of shares;
(n) Provisions relating to the transfer of shares;
(o) Matters relating to the increase or decrease of share capital;
(p) If the company is to buy back its own shares, such matter;
(q) Appointment of the company secretary;
(r) Provisions relating to the remuneration, allowances and facilities of directors;

दफा २०: नियमावली (Articles of Association)
capital;
(p) If the company is to buy back its own shares, such matter;
(q) Appointment of the company secretary;
(r) Provisions relating to the remuneration, allowances and facilities of directors;
(s) Use of the company's seal, if it is to be used in its transactions;
(t) Accounts, books of account and audit of the company;
(u) Provisions relating to the raising of loans or debentures;
(v) Matters relating to the merger of the company;
(w) If the prevailing law requires any matter to be disclosed in the articles of association of a company carrying on any particular business, such matter;
(x) Other necessary matters to be disclosed in the articles of association.
(3) Any provision contained in the articles of association, including any provision relating to the protection of a director or officer of the company, which is inconsistent with this Act and the memorandum of association, shall be void to the extent of such inconsistency.
(4) The format of the articles of association shall be as prescribed.

दफा २१: प्रबन्धपत्र वा नियमावलीमा संशोधन (Amendment of memorandum of association or articles of association)
apply to the Office for prior approval along with the prescribed fee, and if the Office gives approval to amend the name as per the application so received, the name of the company shall be amended.
(4) If a shareholder of a public company is not satisfied with the amendment made to the objectives of the company, he/she may, stating the reasons therefor, apply to the Court to have such amendment declared invalid, upon fulfilling the following conditions:
(a) The application shall be filed by a shareholder or shareholders holding at least five percent of the paid-up capital of the company, other than the shareholders who consented to or voted for the amendment or change;
(b) The application shall be filed within twenty-one days after the date on which the resolution to amend the objectives of the company was passed;
(c) Where an application is to be filed on behalf of one or more shareholders entitled to file an application, the person authorized in writing for that purpose shall file the application.

दफा २१: प्रबन्धपत्र वा नियमावलीमा संशोधन (Amendment of memorandum of association or articles of association)
the Court may issue an appropriate order by specifying the following terms and conditions:
(a) To declare the amendment made to the objectives of the company as valid or invalid, in whole or in part;
(b) To cause the company to purchase the shares and other rights held by the shareholders who filed the application pursuant to sub-section (4) due to disagreement with the change in the main objectives of the company, at a fair price;
(c) While purchasing shares pursuant to clause (b), the purchase shall be made from the amount mentioned in sub-section (2) of Section 61, and in the case of a company which does not have such amount, to issue an order to reduce the capital of the company in such a way that the company passes a special resolution and the share capital is deemed to have been reduced to the extent of the shares so purchased, and where such order is issued, the company shall amend its memorandum of association and articles of association subject to the provisions of this Act.

दफा २९: प्रिमियम मूल्यको शेयर जारी गर्न सकिने (Issue of shares at premium)
ssue of securities pursuant to the prevailing law relating to securities may issue shares at a premium with the approval of the general meeting in a situation where its assets exceed its liabilities.
(2) Where shares are sold at a premium pursuant to sub-section (1), the amount exceeding the face value out of the proceeds shall be deposited into a premium account to be opened for that purpose.
(3) The company may use the amount in the account pursuant to sub-section (2) for the following purposes:
(a) To allot and issue fully paid-up bonus shares to the shareholders out of the unissued share capital;
(b) To provide for the premium payable on the redemption of any redeemable preference shares;
(c) To write off the preliminary expenses of the company;
(d) To bear or reimburse the expenses incurred or commission or discount paid in connection with the issuance of shares of the company.
(4) While seeking approval of the Office to issue shares at a premium pursuant to sub-section (1), audited financial statements for three years shall be provided to the Office.

