दफा ३६: डिबेञ्चर ट्रष्टी र कम्पनीबीच सम्झौता हुनु पर्ने (Agreement to be entered into between debenture trustee and company)
गर्न गराउन सक्नेछ ।
(५) यस दफा बमोजिम डिबेञ्चर ट्रष्टी र कम्पनीको बीचमा सम्झौता भइसकेपछि त्यस्तो कम्पनीले थप डिबेञ्चर उठाउने भएमा डिबेञ्चर ट्रष्टीको स्वीकृति लिनु पर्नेछ ।

**English Translation:**

36. Agreement to be entered into between debenture trustee and company: (1) In respect of debentures to be raised by any company, an agreement shall be entered into between the company issuing debentures and the debenture trustee acting as a trustee for the protection of the interests of the debenture-holders.
(2) While entering into an agreement pursuant to sub-section (1), the following matters shall be disclosed in such agreement:
(a) That the debenture trustee may make or cause to be made valuation of the assets, project analysis or management analysis of the company;
(b) The time for payment of the principal and interest of the debentures purchased by the debenture-holders, the interest rate, the procedure for payment of principal and interest, and matters relating to the conversion of debentures into shares, if any;
(c) Matters relating to the rights of other creditors in the assets of the company and the provisions made in respect of liabilities to arise in the future;

दफा ३६: डिबेञ्चर ट्रष्टी र कम्पनीबीच सम्झौता हुनु पर्ने (Agreement to be entered into between debenture trustee and company)
version of debentures into shares, if any;
(c) Matters relating to the rights of other creditors in the assets of the company and the provisions made in respect of liabilities to arise in the future;
(d) That if the terms mentioned in the agreement are violated or not fulfilled, or if the financial transactions of the company are to be taken under control for any other reasonable reason, or if the security according to the agreement is to be taken into possession, the debenture trustee may take possession of the assets or property of such company or the property taken by the debenture trustee as security, or keep the security itself or sell it through auction or other appropriate manner;
(e) Matters relating to the procedure for payment of service fees and other direct expenses of the debenture trustee by the company;
(f) That the debenture trustee shall not bear responsibility for any loss or damage caused to the company or the debenture-holders while acting in the capacity of a debenture trustee;

दफा ३६: डिबेञ्चर ट्रष्टी र कम्पनीबीच सम्झौता हुनु पर्ने (Agreement to be entered into between debenture trustee and company)
by the company;
(f) That the debenture trustee shall not bear responsibility for any loss or damage caused to the company or the debenture-holders while acting in the capacity of a debenture trustee;
(g) The legal actions that the debenture trustee may take on behalf of the debenture-holders and the exercise of the rights of the debenture-holders in the event of the dissolution of the company;
(h) Other necessary matters relating to the protection of the interests of the debenture-holders.
(3) The debenture trustee may take the assets of the company as security for the protection of the interests of the debenture-holders and have such security transferred to its name according to the prevailing law.
(4) Before taking security pursuant to sub-section (3), the debenture trustee may, if it deems necessary, make or cause to be made valuation of the property or assets to be taken as security and project analysis or management analysis of the company.
(5) After an agreement has been entered into between the debenture trustee and the company pursuant to this Section, the company shall obtain the approval of the debenture trustee if it is to raise further debentures.

दफा ३७: डिबेञ्चर ट्रष्टीले जाँचबुझ गर्न र विवरण माग गर्न सक्ने (Debenture trustee may inquire and call for details)
िति छ वा छैन,
(घ) कम्पनीका अन्य साहू तथा दायित्वहरु सम्बन्धी विषय,
(ङ) कम्पनीको वासलात तथा लेखापरीक्षकको प्रतिवेदन,
(च) डिबेञ्चर ट्रष्टीले उपयुक्त ठानेको अन्य आवश्यक विषय ।

**English Translation:**

37. Debenture trustee may inquire and call for details: Before entering into an agreement with a company to act as a debenture trustee, the debenture trustee may make necessary inquiries and take or call for details, notices or information on the following matters, and if so called for, the concerned company shall provide the same:
(a) Whether or not there is a provision in the memorandum of association or articles of association of the company to raise loans or debentures, and if there is such a provision, whether or not the board of directors of the company has the power to make a decision to raise debentures;
(b) Whether or not there is a provision to raise debentures through a debenture trustee according to the memorandum of association or articles of association of the company;
(c) Whether or not the existing assets of the company are sufficient to cover the value of the debentures to be raised;
(d) Matters relating to other creditors and liabilities of the company;

दफा ३७: डिबेञ्चर ट्रष्टीले जाँचबुझ गर्न र विवरण माग गर्न सक्ने (Debenture trustee may inquire and call for details)
ompany;
(c) Whether or not the existing assets of the company are sufficient to cover the value of the debentures to be raised;
(d) Matters relating to other creditors and liabilities of the company;
(e) The balance sheet and audit report of the company;
(f) Other necessary matters deemed appropriate by the debenture trustee.

दफा ४६: शेयरधनी र डिबेञ्चरवालाको दर्ता किताब (Register of shareholders and debenture-holders)
ञ्चालक, पदाधिकारी तथा कर्मचारीलाई दफा १६० मा उल्लिखित दण्ड जरिवानाका अतिरिक्त झुट्टा अभिलेख राखिएको कारणबाट पुग्न गएको हानि नोक्सानी समेत सम्बन्धित पक्षले भराई लिन पाउनेछ ।

**English Translation:**

46. Register of shareholders and debenture-holders: (1) Every company shall maintain a register of shareholders and a register of debenture-holders in the prescribed format at its registered office.
(2) The register of shareholders pursuant to sub-section (1) shall state the following matters in respect of each shareholder according to the serial number of shares:
(a) The full name and address of the shareholder;
(b) The number of shares held by the shareholder;
(c) The total amount paid by the shareholder for the shares and the amount remaining to be paid;
(d) The date on which his/her name was entered as a shareholder;
(e) The date on which his/her name was removed;
(f) If any person is nominated to have a right in the shares after the death of the shareholder, the name and address of such person.
(3) The register of debenture-holders pursuant to sub-section (1) shall state the following matters in respect of each debenture-holder according to the serial number of debentures:

दफा ४६: शेयरधनी र डिबेञ्चरवालाको दर्ता किताब (Register of shareholders and debenture-holders)
s of such person.
(3) The register of debenture-holders pursuant to sub-section (1) shall state the following matters in respect of each debenture-holder according to the serial number of debentures:
(a) The full name and address of the debenture-holder;
(b) The number of debentures held by the debenture-holder;
(c) The total amount paid by the debenture-holder for the debentures and the amount remaining to be paid;
(d) The date on which his/her name was entered as a debenture-holder;
(e) The date on which his/her name was removed;
(f) If any person is nominated to have a right in the debentures after the death of the debenture-holder, the name and address of such person.
(4) If a shareholder or debenture-holder of a company wishes to inspect the register maintained pursuant to sub-section (1), the company shall allow such inspection.

दफा ५१: शेयर, डिबेञ्चर र ऋणको लगत (Records of shares, debentures and loans)
कम्पनीले दफा ७८ बमोजिम पेश गर्नु पर्ने प्रतिवेदनमा उपदफा (२) बमोजिमका विवरणहरु समेत उल्लेख गरेको भए त्यस्तो कम्पनीले यस दफा बमोजिम छुट्टै लगत कार्यालयमा पठाउनु पर्ने छैन ।

**English Translation:**

51. Records of shares, debentures and loans: (1) Every company shall, twenty-one days before the annual general meeting, prepare and maintain a record of the shareholders and debenture-holders existing for the time being and those whose names have been removed, up to thirty days before the annual general meeting.
(2) The record pursuant to sub-section (1) shall, in addition to other matters, disclose the following:
(a) The authorized capital of the company and the number of shares;
(b) The issued share capital of the company;
(c) The paid-up capital of the company;
(d) The amount called on each share;
(e) The total amount of installments collected;
(f) The total amount remaining to be collected;
(g) The total amount paid as brokerage fee on shares or debentures;
(h) Where any shares have been forfeited, the total number of such shares, the reason for and date of forfeiture;

दफा ५१: शेयर, डिबेञ्चर र ऋणको लगत (Records of shares, debentures and loans)
to be collected;
(g) The total amount paid as brokerage fee on shares or debentures;
(h) Where any shares have been forfeited, the total number of such shares, the reason for and date of forfeiture;
(i) The loans taken from banks, financial institutions or any other persons or the guarantees given by the company;
(i1) If investment has been made in the shares or debentures of other companies, the name and registration number of such company and the amount of investment made in the shares or debentures;
(j) The names and addresses of the directors for the time being.
(3) The record pursuant to sub-section (1) shall be signed by at least one director and sent to the Office within thirty days from the date of the annual general meeting of the company, and in the case of a company which does not hold an annual general meeting, within one year from the date of obtaining approval if it carries on a business requiring approval from the concerned body under the prevailing law, or within one year from the date of registration if such approval is not required.

दफा ५६: शेयर पूँजी हेरफेर गर्ने कम्पनीको अधिकार (Power of company to alter share capital)
shareholders of the company shall not have the first right to purchase the following shares to be issued by the company:
(a) Shares to be issued by the company for any consideration other than cash;
(b) Shares issued to any person under any right or facility granted in accordance with the terms of an agreement with the company;
(c) Shares issued under an employee share scheme;
(d) Shares issued in accordance with an agreement between a company and its creditors;
(e) Shares created when a company converts preference shares into ordinary shares or debentures into shares;
(f) Shares issued in accordance with an agreement entered into between the concerned parties in the course of restructuring the management, capital or debt of the company, or in the course of implementing a restructuring program approved under the prevailing law relating to insolvency, or in the course of implementing a program for the merger of one public company into another public company.
(10) A company shall not increase its share capital or issue bonus shares by revaluing the assets of the company, except from the profits earned by the company or from a fund created out of such profits.

दफा ६१: कम्पनीले आफ्नो शेयर आफैंले खरिद गर्न नहुने (Company not to buy back its own shares)
in the following circumstances:
(a) If the entire amount of shares issued by the company has been paid up;
(b) If the shares issued by a public company have been registered with the Securities Board;
(c) If there is a provision in the articles of association of the concerned company allowing it to buy back its own shares;
(d) If a special resolution has been passed in the general meeting of the concerned company allowing it to buy back its own shares;
(e) If the amount of debt to be paid by the company does not exceed double the ratio of its capital and general reserve fund after the company has bought back its own shares;
Explanation: For the purpose of this clause, "debt amount" means the entire secured and unsecured loan amount taken by the company.
(f) If the amount of its own shares to be purchased by the company does not exceed twenty percent of the total paid-up capital and general reserve fund of the company;
(g) If it is not contrary to the directives issued by the Office from time to time in relation to the buyback of its own shares.

दफा ६१: कम्पनीले आफ्नो शेयर आफैंले खरिद गर्न नहुने (Company not to buy back its own shares)
of the total paid-up capital and general reserve fund of the company;
(g) If it is not contrary to the directives issued by the Office from time to time in relation to the buyback of its own shares.
(3) The resolution to be placed before the general meeting pursuant to clause (d) of sub-section (2) shall contain the following particulars:
(a) The reason for and necessity of buying back its own shares;
(b) A description of the assessment of the possible impact on the financial position of the concerned company due to the buyback of its own shares;
(c) The type and number of shares proposed to be purchased;
(d) The maximum or minimum amount required to purchase the shares pursuant to clause (c) and its financial source;
(e) The period within which its own shares can be bought back;
(f) The method of purchasing shares;
(g) Other necessary matters prescribed by the Office and required to be disclosed under the prevailing law in relation to the buyback of its own shares.

दफा ६१: कम्पनीले आफ्नो शेयर आफैंले खरिद गर्न नहुने (Company not to buy back its own shares)
ght back;
(f) The method of purchasing shares;
(g) Other necessary matters prescribed by the Office and required to be disclosed under the prevailing law in relation to the buyback of its own shares.
(4) If a special resolution pursuant to sub-section (3) is passed by the general meeting, the concerned company may buy back its own shares by any of the following means within twelve months from the date of passing of such resolution:
(a) By purchasing through the stock exchange;
(b) By purchasing from the employees the shares allotted to them;
(c) By purchasing proportionately from the existing shareholders.
(5) If a company buys back its own shares pursuant to sub-section (4), it shall inform the Office of the number of shares bought back, the amount paid therefor and other necessary particulars within thirty days from the date of such buyback.
(6) An amount equivalent to the face value of the shares bought back by the company pursuant to sub-section (4) shall be deposited into a separate capital redemption reserve fund to be created for that purpose, and the amount of such fund shall be maintained as paid-up capital.

दफा ६५: अग्राधिकार शेयर (Preference shares)
to ordinary shares;
(b) The percentage of dividends to be received by preference shareholders;
(c) Whether dividends are cumulative or non-cumulative (i.e., distributed only in profit-making years);
(d) Whether or not preference is to be given in refunding the share amount in the event of liquidation of the company;
(e) Whether or not there are voting rights, and if there are voting rights, whether they are only on matters relating to preference shares or also on other matters;
(f) If there are voting rights on other matters pursuant to clause (e), the proportion in which such voting rights are to be exercised;
(g) Whether or not they are convertible into ordinary shares;
(h) Whether the preference share amount is redeemable after a certain period or irredeemable;
(i) Whether the preference shares are to be redeemed with or without a premium.
(4) If any preference shares are issued on the condition of redemption, such shares shall not be redeemable until their full value has been paid up.

दफा ७८: कार्यालयमा प्रतिवेदन पेश गर्नु पर्ने (Report to be submitted to Office)
्चको विवरण,
(ढ) शेयरधनीहरुले बुझिलिन बाँकी रहेको लाभांशको रकम,
(ण) कम्पनीले यस ऐन तथा प्रचलित कानूनको पालना पूर्ण रुपमा गरेको छ भन्ने कुराको उद्घोषण,
(त) अन्य आवश्यक कुरा ।

**English Translation:**

78. Report to be submitted to Office: Every public company shall prepare a report disclosing the following matters and submit it to the Office at least twenty-one days prior to the annual general meeting. Such report shall be approved by the board of directors and certified by the auditor of the company:
(a) The number of shares allotted;
(b) The number of paid-up and unpaid shares among the allotted shares;
(c) The details of the directors, managing directors, auditors, chief executives, managers of the company and the amount of remuneration, allowances and facilities paid to them;
(d) The names of persons or body corporates who have purchased five percent or more of the paid-up capital of the company and the details of shares or debentures held in their names;
(e) The total amount received from the sale of shares and the details of new shares and debentures purchased and issued by the company in the concerned financial year;

दफा ७८: कार्यालयमा प्रतिवेदन पेश गर्नु पर्ने (Report to be submitted to Office)
debentures held in their names;
(e) The total amount received from the sale of shares and the details of new shares and debentures purchased and issued by the company in the concerned financial year;
(f) The amount remaining to be paid by a director or substantial shareholder or his/her close relative to the company;
(g) The amount paid or payable for the sale of shares or any other work;
(h) The amount of principal and interest of loans taken from banks and financial institutions and remaining to be paid;
(i) The amount claimed to be received by the company or to be paid by the company to other persons, or the details of any lawsuit pending in this regard;
(j) The number of employees or workers engaged in the management and other levels of the company;
(k) The number of foreigners engaged in the management and other levels of the company and the remuneration, allowances and facilities paid to them;

दफा ७८: कार्यालयमा प्रतिवेदन पेश गर्नु पर्ने (Report to be submitted to Office)
in the management and other levels of the company;
(k) The number of foreigners engaged in the management and other levels of the company and the remuneration, allowances and facilities paid to them;
(l) If any agreement has been entered into between the company and any foreign body or persons for investment, management or technical services or other matters for a period exceeding one year, the details thereof and the details of dividends, commissions, fees, charges and royalties, etc., paid in the concerned financial year pursuant to such agreement;
(m) The details of the management expenses of the company for one financial year;
(n) The amount of dividends remaining to be received by the shareholders;
(o) A declaration that the company has fully complied with this Act and the prevailing law;
(p) Other necessary matters.

दफा ८१: विवरण नपठाएमा जरिवाना हुने (Penalty for not submitting report)
ers of the following companies who fail to provide the report, notice, information or reply pursuant to Section 51, 78, 80, 120, 131 or 156 within the period mentioned in sub-section (1), as follows:
(a) For a period of up to three months from the expiry of the period, if the company has a paid-up capital of up to two million five hundred thousand rupees, a fine of one thousand rupees; if the company has a paid-up capital of up to ten million rupees, a fine of two thousand rupees; and if the company has a paid-up capital of more than ten million rupees, a fine of five thousand rupees;
(b) For an additional period of up to three months from the date of expiry of the period mentioned in clause (a), if the company has a paid-up capital of up to two million five hundred thousand rupees, a fine of one thousand five hundred rupees; if the company has a paid-up capital of up to ten million rupees, a fine of three thousand rupees; and if the company has a paid-up capital of more than ten million rupees, a fine of seven thousand rupees;

दफा ८१: विवरण नपठाएमा जरिवाना हुने (Penalty for not submitting report)
company has a paid-up capital of up to ten million rupees, a fine of three thousand rupees; and if the company has a paid-up capital of more than ten million rupees, a fine of seven thousand rupees;
(c) For an additional period of up to six months after the expiry of the period mentioned in clause (b), if the company has a paid-up capital of up to two million five hundred thousand rupees, a fine of two thousand five hundred rupees; if the company has a paid-up capital of up to ten million rupees, a fine of five thousand rupees; and if the company has a paid-up capital of more than ten million rupees, a fine of ten thousand rupees;
(d) If the period mentioned in clause (c) has also expired, if the company has a paid-up capital of up to two million five hundred thousand rupees, a fine of five thousand rupees for each year; if the company has a paid-up capital of up to ten million rupees, a fine of ten thousand rupees for each year; and if the company has a paid-up capital of more than ten million rupees, a fine of twenty thousand rupees for each year.

दफा ८३: विशेष प्रस्ताव पेश गर्नु पर्ने (Special resolution to be submitted)
(ज) प्राइभेट कम्पनी पब्लिक कम्पनीमा वा पब्लिक कम्पनी प्राइभेट कम्पनीमा परिणत हुने विषय,
(झ) यस ऐन वा नियमावलीमा कम्पनीले विशेष प्रस्ताव पारित गर्नु पर्ने भनिएको अन्य विषय ।

**English Translation:**

83. Special resolution to be submitted: A special resolution shall be submitted to the general meeting of the company for making decisions on the following matters:
(a) Matters relating to increasing the authorized capital of the company;
(b) Matters relating to reducing or altering the share capital of the company;
(c) Matters relating to changing the name or main objectives of the company;
(d) Matters relating to the merger of one company into another company;
(e) Matters relating to the issue of bonus shares;
(f) Matters relating to the buyback of its own shares by the company;
(g) Matters relating to the sale of shares at a discount;
(h) Matters relating to the conversion of a private company into a public company or a public company into a private company;
(i) Other matters for which the company is required to pass a special resolution in this Act or the articles of association.

दफा ८४: शेयरधनीहरुलाई संक्षिप्त आर्थिक विवरण पठाउने व्यवस्था (Provision for sending abridged financial statements to shareholders)
Provided, however, that when sending the notice of the annual general meeting, an abridged annual financial statement prepared pursuant to sub-sections (2) and (3) shall be sent to each shareholder.
(2) The abridged financial statement to be sent pursuant to the proviso to sub-section (1) shall be prepared on the basis of the company's annual financial statements and directors' report. The format of such statement shall be as prescribed by the Office on the basis of the recommendation of the body designated to determine accounting standards according to the prevailing law.
(3) The abridged annual financial statement shall, in addition to other matters, disclose the following:
(a) The fact that the abridged annual financial statement is only a summary of the company's annual financial statements and directors' report;
(b) The auditor's opinion as to whether or not the abridged annual financial statement is in conformity with the company's annual financial statements and directors' report, and whether or not such statement is in conformity with the format prescribed under this Section;

दफा ८४: शेयरधनीहरुलाई संक्षिप्त आर्थिक विवरण पठाउने व्यवस्था (Provision for sending abridged financial statements to shareholders)
cial statement is in conformity with the company's annual financial statements and directors' report, and whether or not such statement is in conformity with the format prescribed under this Section;
(c) Whether or not the auditor has made any qualification in respect of the company's annual financial statements, and if any qualification has been made, the full details of such qualification and the materials required to understand such qualification;
(d) The full details relating to the auditor's report if the auditor has stated in his/her report that the company's accounts and accounting records are incomplete or that the company's accounts do not conform to the records and statements maintained by the company or that the information and explanations called for have not been received.
(4) Instead of sending the abridged annual financial statement to the personal address of the shareholders pursuant to sub-section (1), the company may publish it in a national level daily newspaper at least twice at the time of publishing the notice of the meeting on that matter.

दफा ८९: सञ्चालकको पदमा नियुक्त हुन वा बहाल रहन नसक्ने अवस्था (Circumstances in which a person cannot be appointed or remain in office as director)
यम रहेको भएमा ।
(४) कुनै व्यक्तिलाई सञ्चालकको पदमा नियुक्त हुन वा बहाल रहन अयोग्य ठहर्याउनु अघि कम्पनीले निजलाई सो कुराको सूचना दिई सफाई पेश गर्ने मनासिब मौका दिनु पर्नेछ ।

**English Translation:**

89. Circumstances in which a person cannot be appointed or remain in office as director: (1) None of the following persons shall be appointed as a director:
(a) In the case of a public company, a person who has not attained twenty-one years of age;
(b) A person of unsound mind or a lunatic;
(c) A person who has been declared insolvent and a period of five years has not elapsed since such declaration;
(d) A person who has been punished for corruption or any other offense involving moral turpitude;
Provided, however, that in the case of a private company, a period of three years has not elapsed since the date of payment of such punishment;
(e) A person who has been convicted of theft, fraud, forgery or unauthorized misappropriation or misuse of property entrusted to him/her and a period of three years has not elapsed since the date of payment of such punishment;
(f) A person who has any personal interest in the business of the concerned company or in any contract or transaction;

दफा ८९: सञ्चालकको पदमा नियुक्त हुन वा बहाल रहन नसक्ने अवस्था (Circumstances in which a person cannot be appointed or remain in office as director)
iod of three years has not elapsed since the date of payment of such punishment;
(f) A person who has any personal interest in the business of the concerned company or in any contract or transaction;
(g) A person who is serving as a director, substantial shareholder, employee, auditor or advisor of another company having similar objectives, or who has any personal interest in such company;
Provided, however, that such person of a private company may be a director in another private company having similar objectives.
(h) A shareholder who has been found to be liable to pay any amount to the concerned company;
(i) In the case of a person punished under Section 160, a period of one year has not elapsed since the date of punishment, or in the case of a person punished under Section 161, a period of six months has not elapsed since the date of punishment;
(j) In the case of a company carrying on any particular business, a person who does not possess the qualifications prescribed by the prevailing law or who has any disqualification prescribed by such law;

दफा ८९: सञ्चालकको पदमा नियुक्त हुन वा बहाल रहन नसक्ने अवस्था (Circumstances in which a person cannot be appointed or remain in office as director)
In the case of a company carrying on any particular business, a person who does not possess the qualifications prescribed by the prevailing law or who has any disqualification prescribed by such law;
(k) A person who is a director of a company that has not submitted the reports and statements required to be submitted to the Office under this Act for three consecutive financial years;
(k1) A person who has outstanding fine amount to be paid pursuant to sub-section (2) of Section 81;
(l) A person who is serving as a director of another listed company and receives remuneration or any facility other than meeting allowance and actual expenses incurred for coming, going and staying at the meeting place.
(2) None of the following persons shall be appointed as an independent director:
(a) A person as mentioned in sub-section (1);
(b) A shareholder of the concerned company;

दफा ८९: सञ्चालकको पदमा नियुक्त हुन वा बहाल रहन नसक्ने अवस्था (Circumstances in which a person cannot be appointed or remain in office as director)
taying at the meeting place.
(2) None of the following persons shall be appointed as an independent director:
(a) A person as mentioned in sub-section (1);
(b) A shareholder of the concerned company;
(c) A person who has not obtained at least a graduate degree in a subject related to the business of the concerned company and has at least ten years of experience in the relevant field or in company management, or who has not obtained at least a graduate degree in economics, finance, management, accounting, statistics, commerce, business administration or law and has at least ten years of experience in the relevant field;
(d) A person who has not completed three years since his/her retirement from the post of officer, auditor or employee of the concerned company;
(e) A close relative of an officer of the concerned company;
(f) The auditor of the concerned company or his/her partner.
(3) No person shall remain in office as a director in the following circumstances:
(a) If he/she is in a circumstance where he/she cannot be appointed as a director as mentioned in sub-section (1) or (2);
(b) If the general meeting passes a resolution to remove him/her from the office of director;

दफा ८९: सञ्चालकको पदमा नियुक्त हुन वा बहाल रहन नसक्ने अवस्था (Circumstances in which a person cannot be appointed or remain in office as director)
in a circumstance where he/she cannot be appointed as a director as mentioned in sub-section (1) or (2);
(b) If the general meeting passes a resolution to remove him/her from the office of director;
(c) If the resignation submitted by the director from his/her office is approved by the board of directors;
(d) If it is proved by the Court that he/she has committed dishonesty or bad faith in the affairs of the company;
(e) If it is proved by the Court that the director has committed any act prohibited by this Act or has failed to perform any act required by this Act;
(f) If he/she has been blacklisted by an authorized body for non-payment of a loan from a bank or financial institution under the prevailing law and the period of blacklisting is still in effect.
(4) Before declaring any person ineligible to be appointed or to remain in office as a director, the company shall give him/her notice thereof and a reasonable opportunity to present his/her defense.

दफा ९३: सञ्चालकको संलग्नता रहेको कम्पनीसँगको कारोबार (Transactions with company in which director has interest)
pay compensation for the same.
(3) Notwithstanding anything contained elsewhere in this Section, the provisions of sub-section (1) shall not apply in respect of in-kind property acquired as follows:
(a) When a holding company acquires such property from its wholly-owned subsidiary company;
(b) When a wholly-owned subsidiary company of a holding company acquires such property from another wholly-owned subsidiary company of the same holding company;
(c) When carrying out transactions at prevailing market prices in the ordinary course of business of the company.

दफा ९४: सञ्चालकले शेयर बारेमा जानकारी गराउनु पर्ने (Directors to provide information about shares)
in the shares or debentures of the company in which he/she is a director or its subsidiary or holding company or any other subsidiary company of the holding company, or if his/her right is to cease;
(b) If he/she enters into any agreement to sell the shares or debentures mentioned in clause (a) registered in his/her name;
(c) If the company in which he/she is a director transfers to anyone else the right granted to purchase the shares or debentures of such company;
(d) If a subsidiary or holding company of the company in which he/she is a director, or a subsidiary company of such company or any other subsidiary company of the holding company, grants the right to purchase the shares or debentures of such company;
(e) If he/she transfers to anyone else the right to purchase the shares or debentures of the company mentioned in clause (d).
(3) While sending information to the company pursuant to sub-section (2), the number, amount and class of shares or debentures shall be clearly stated.
(4) The company shall maintain a separate register for recording the information received pursuant to sub-sections (2) and (3).

दफा ९५: सञ्चालक समितिको अधिकार र कर्तव्य (Powers and duties of Board of Directors)
company may recover from a director or representative any loss or damage caused to the company by any act done by him/her in the capacity of a director or representative exceeding his/her authority.
(5) If any person knowingly or having reason to believe that a director or representative pursuant to sub-section (3) is about to carry out any transaction for his/her personal benefit or to cause loss or damage to the company, enters into any transaction with such director or representative, such person shall not be entitled to make any claim against the company in respect of such transaction.
(6) Notwithstanding anything contained in sub-section (3), the board of directors shall not be entitled to delegate the following powers conferred on the company, and such powers shall be exercised only in accordance with the decisions passed by the meeting of the board of directors:
(a) The power to call for payment of amounts remaining to be paid by shareholders for shares;
(b) The power to issue debentures;
(c) The power to take loans or borrowings by means other than debentures;
(d) The power to invest the amount in the company's fund;
(e) The power to grant loans.

दफा ९५: सञ्चालक समितिको अधिकार र कर्तव्य (Powers and duties of Board of Directors)
s;
(b) The power to issue debentures;
(c) The power to take loans or borrowings by means other than debentures;
(d) The power to invest the amount in the company's fund;
(e) The power to grant loans.
(7) The provisions of clause (e) of sub-section (6) shall not apply in the case of loans granted and deposits received by banking and financial companies in the ordinary course of business.
(8) If the board of directors deems it necessary to constitute a sub-committee to carry out any particular work, it may constitute one or more sub-committees as required and cause such work to be carried out.

दफा १०९: वार्षिक आर्थिक विवरण र सञ्चालक समितिको प्रतिवेदन तयार गर्नु पर्ने (Annual financial statements and directors' report to be prepared)
nths of the end of the financial year:
(a) Balance sheet as of the last date of the financial year;
(b) Profit and loss account for the financial year;
(c) Cash flow statement for the financial year.
(2) The annual financial statements to be prepared pursuant to sub-section (1) shall show the true and fair view of the company's transactions up to the end of the concerned financial year and shall also include the profit and loss account and cash flow statement for that financial year. Such financial statements shall be prepared in the format prescribed by the prevailing law.
(3) The annual financial statements pursuant to sub-section (1) shall be approved by the board of directors and audited.
(4) The board of directors of every public company or every private company with a paid-up capital of ten million rupees or more or with an annual turnover of one hundred million rupees or more shall, in addition to the annual financial statements to be prepared pursuant to sub-section (1), also prepare a separate report of the board of directors within the same period, disclosing the following particulars:
(a) Overview of the transactions of the previous year;

दफा १०९: वार्षिक आर्थिक विवरण र सञ्चालक समितिको प्रतिवेदन तयार गर्नु पर्ने (Annual financial statements and directors' report to be prepared)
suant to sub-section (1), also prepare a separate report of the board of directors within the same period, disclosing the following particulars:
(a) Overview of the transactions of the previous year;
(b) The impact, if any, of national and international circumstances on the company's transactions;
(c) The opinion of the board of directors regarding the achievements of the current year up to the date of preparation of the report and matters to be done in the future;
(d) Industrial or business relations of the company;
(e) Changes in the board of directors and the reasons therefor;
(f) Key matters affecting the transactions;
(g) The response of the board of directors to any qualification mentioned in the audit report;
(h) The amount recommended for dividend distribution;
(i) If shares have been forfeited, the number of shares forfeited, their face value, the total amount received by the company for such shares before forfeiture, and the amount received by the company from the sale of such shares after forfeiture, and if any amount has been refunded for the forfeited shares, the details thereof;

दफा १०९: वार्षिक आर्थिक विवरण र सञ्चालक समितिको प्रतिवेदन तयार गर्नु पर्ने (Annual financial statements and directors' report to be prepared)
such shares before forfeiture, and the amount received by the company from the sale of such shares after forfeiture, and if any amount has been refunded for the forfeited shares, the details thereof;
(j) Review of the progress of the transactions of the company and its subsidiary company in the previous financial year and the position at the end of that financial year;
(k) Major transactions completed by the company and its subsidiary company in the financial year and any significant changes in the company's transactions during that period;
(l) Information provided by the substantial shareholders of the company to the company in the previous financial year;
(m) Details of share ownership of the directors and officers of the company in the previous financial year and information received by the company from them regarding their involvement in the company's share transactions, if any;
(n) Details of information provided regarding the personal interest of any director and his/her close relative in agreements related to the company in the previous financial year;

दफा १०९: वार्षिक आर्थिक विवरण र सञ्चालक समितिको प्रतिवेदन तयार गर्नु पर्ने (Annual financial statements and directors' report to be prepared)
ansactions, if any;
(n) Details of information provided regarding the personal interest of any director and his/her close relative in agreements related to the company in the previous financial year;
(o) If the company has bought back its own shares, the reason for such buyback, the number and face value of such shares, and the amount paid by the company for such buyback;
(p) Whether or not there is an internal control system, and if there is, a detailed description thereof;
(q) Details of the total management expenses for the previous financial year;
(r) Names of the members of the audit committee, their remuneration, allowances and facilities received, details of the work done by the committee and details of any recommendations made by the committee;
(s) If any amount is due to the company from a director, managing director, chief executive, substantial shareholder of the company or his/her close relative or a firm, company or body corporate in which he/she is involved, such matter;
(t) The amount of remuneration, allowances and facilities paid to directors, managing directors, chief executives and officers;

दफा १०९: वार्षिक आर्थिक विवरण र सञ्चालक समितिको प्रतिवेदन तयार गर्नु पर्ने (Annual financial statements and directors' report to be prepared)
rm, company or body corporate in which he/she is involved, such matter;
(t) The amount of remuneration, allowances and facilities paid to directors, managing directors, chief executives and officers;
(u) The amount of dividends remaining to be received by the shareholders;
(v) Details of purchase or sale of assets pursuant to Section 141;
(w) Details of transactions between related companies pursuant to Section 175;
(x) Any other matter required to be disclosed in the directors' report pursuant to this Act and the prevailing law;
(y) Other necessary matters.
(5) While preparing the annual financial statements pursuant to sub-section (1), in the case of the year of incorporation of the company, it shall include the period from the date of incorporation to the end of that financial year, and in subsequent years, it shall also include the accounts of the previous financial year.
(6) The annual financial statements prepared pursuant to this Section shall be kept open for inspection by any shareholder who wishes to inspect them.

दफा ११२: लेखापरीक्षकमा नियुक्त हुन नसक्ने (Ineligibility for appointment as auditor)
अयोग्य भएमा वा कम्पनीको लेखापरीक्षक नियुक्त हुन वा कायम रहन नसक्ने स्थिति उत्पन्न भएमा निजले लेखापरीक्षण गर्नु पर्ने वा गरिरहेको काम तत्काल रोकी सो कुराको जानकारी लिखित रुपमा कम्पनीलाई दिनु पर्नेछ ।
(४) यस दफाको प्रतिकूल हुने गरी नियुक्त भएको लेखापरीक्षकले गरेको लेखापरीक्षण मान्य हुने छैन ।

**English Translation:**

112. Ineligibility for appointment as auditor: (1) The following persons or a firm or company in which such persons are partners shall not be appointed as auditor, and if already appointed, shall not remain in office:
(a) A director of the company, a consultant appointed to receive regular remuneration or cash facilities, a person or employee or worker in the management group of the company, or a partner of any of them, or an employee of any such partner, or a close relative of a director or partner among them, or his/her employee;
(b) A debtor who has taken a loan from the company in any manner, or a person who has not paid any amount due to the company within the stipulated period, or a close relative of such person;
(c) A person who has been punished for an offense related to audit and a period of three years has not elapsed since the payment of such punishment;

दफा ११२: लेखापरीक्षकमा नियुक्त हुन नसक्ने (Ineligibility for appointment as auditor)
ulated period, or a close relative of such person;
(c) A person who has been punished for an offense related to audit and a period of three years has not elapsed since the payment of such punishment;
(d) A person who has been declared insolvent;
(e) A substantial shareholder of the company or a shareholder holding one percent or more of the paid-up capital of the company or his/her close relative;
(f) A person who has been punished for corruption, fraud or a criminal offense involving moral turpitude and a period of five years has not elapsed since the payment of such punishment;
(g) A person as mentioned in sub-section (3) of Section 111;
(h) In the case of a public company, a person working full-time or part-time in any government or fully or partially owned or controlled institution of the Government of Nepal or any other company, or his/her partner, or a person working as an employee of such partner, or a person authorized to sign any instrument or report prepared on behalf of the management of the company;
(i) A limited liability company or body corporate;

दफा ४: कम्पनी स्थापनाको लागि निवेदन दिनु पर्ने (Application to be filed for incorporation of company)
रहेको एकल शेयरधनी भएको कम्पनीको स्थापनाको लागि तोकिएको नियमावलीको ढाँचालाई नै संस्थापकले स्वीकार गर्न मञ्जुर गरेमा प्रस्तावित कम्पनीको नियमावली पेश गर्न आवश्यक पर्ने छैन ।

**English Translation:**

4. Application to be filed for incorporation of company: (1) A person wishing to incorporate a company pursuant to Section 3 shall apply to the Office through electronic medium for the approval of the proposed name of the company.
(2) If information is received from the Office that the name of the company has been approved pursuant to sub-section (1), the applicant shall file an application with the Office in the prescribed format by uploading the following documents into the computer system through electronic medium:
(a) The memorandum of association of the proposed company;
(b) The articles of association of the proposed company;
(c) In the case of a public company, a copy of the agreement, if any, entered into between the promoters prior to the incorporation of the company;
(d) In the case of a private company, a copy of the unanimous agreement, if any;

दफा ४: कम्पनी स्थापनाको लागि निवेदन दिनु पर्ने (Application to be filed for incorporation of company)
ompany, a copy of the agreement, if any, entered into between the promoters prior to the incorporation of the company;
(d) In the case of a private company, a copy of the unanimous agreement, if any;
(e) Where the prevailing law requires a prior approval or license from any authority for the registration of a company carrying on any particular type of business or transaction, such approval or license;
(f) Where the promoter is a Nepalese citizen, a certified copy of the citizenship certificate, and where a body corporate is a promoter, the registration certificate of such body, the decision of the board of directors regarding the incorporation of the company and the major instrument relating to the incorporation of such body;
(g) Where a foreign person or company or body is a promoter, the permission obtained under the prevailing law to make investment or carry on business or transaction in Nepal;
(h) Where a foreign person is a promoter, a document proving the citizenship of the country to which he/she belongs;

दफा ४: कम्पनी स्थापनाको लागि निवेदन दिनु पर्ने (Application to be filed for incorporation of company)
he prevailing law to make investment or carry on business or transaction in Nepal;
(h) Where a foreign person is a promoter, a document proving the citizenship of the country to which he/she belongs;
(i) Where a foreign company or body is a promoter, a certified copy of the registration certificate of such company or body and the major instrument relating to its incorporation.
(3) Notwithstanding anything contained in clause (b) of sub-section (2), it shall not be necessary to file the articles of association of the proposed company if the promoter of a company with a single shareholder, where only one person is the promoter, agrees to accept the prescribed format of the articles of association for the incorporation of such company.

दफा ६: कम्पनी दर्ता गर्न इन्कार गर्न सक्ने (Refusal to register company)
ve of the proposed company is contrary to the prevailing law or appears to be improper or undesirable in view of public interest, morality, good conduct, decency, etc., or reflects a criminal intent;
(c) If the name of the proposed company is identical with the name of a company whose registration has been cancelled pursuant to this Act or which has become insolvent under the prevailing law, or so resembles such name as to be likely to create a confusion, and a period of five years has not elapsed since such cancellation of registration or insolvency;
(d) If the requirements for the incorporation of a company under this Act are not fulfilled.
(2) If the Office refuses to register a company in any of the circumstances mentioned in sub-section (1), it shall give a notice thereof, stating the reasons, to the applicant within fifteen days from the date of application for incorporation of the company pursuant to Section 4.
(3) If the Office refuses to register a company pursuant to sub-section (1) or fails to give a notice pursuant to sub-section (2), the person who is not satisfied may file a complaint in the Court within fifteen days.

दफा १८: प्रबन्धपत्र (Memorandum of Association)
्पत्तिको विवरण मूल्याङ्कन गर्दाको आधार उल्लेख गर्नु पर्नेछ ।
(५) प्रबन्धपत्र यस ऐन सँग बाझिएमा बाझिएको हदसम्म स्वतः बदर हुनेछ ।
(६) प्रबन्धपत्रको ढाँचा तोकिए बमोजिम हुनेछ ।

**English Translation:**

18. Memorandum of Association: (1) The memorandum of association of a company shall state the following matters:
(a) The name of the company;
(b) The address of the registered office of the company;
(c) The objectives of the company;
(d) The acts to be carried out to attain the objectives of the company;
(e) The amount of authorized capital of the company, the amount of share capital to be issued by the company for the time being and the amount which the promoters of the company have agreed to pay up;
(f) The types of shares of the company, the rights and powers inherent in such shares, the value of each share and the number of shares of different types;
(g) Any restriction on the purchase or transfer of shares, if any;
(h) The number of shares which the promoters have agreed to take for the time being;
(i) The terms of payment of share amount;
(j) The fact that the liability of the shareholders is limited;
(k) In the case of a private company, the maximum number of shareholders;

दफा १८: प्रबन्धपत्र (Memorandum of Association)
for the time being;
(i) The terms of payment of share amount;
(j) The fact that the liability of the shareholders is limited;
(k) In the case of a private company, the maximum number of shareholders;
(l) Other necessary matters.
(2) In addition to the matters mentioned in sub-section (1), if any of the following matters are to be done or to occur, such matters shall also be mentioned in the memorandum of association:
(a) If a promoter or any other person is to purchase shares or obtain a right in shares for consideration other than cash, such matter;
(b) If the company is to acquire any property in any manner from a promoter or any other person at the time of commencement of its business, such matter;
(c) If the company itself is to bear the expenses incurred in its incorporation, such matter;
(d) If a promoter or any other person is to obtain any special privilege or right from the company, such matter.

दफा २०: नियमावली (Articles of Association)
को बचाउ सम्बन्धमा नियमावलीमा गरिएको कुनै व्यवस्था लगायत यो ऐन तथा प्रबन्धपत्र सँग कुनै व्यवस्था बाझिएमा बाझिएको हदसम्म बदर हुनेछ ।
(४) नियमावलीको ढाँचा तोकिए बमोजिम हुनेछ ।

**English Translation:**

20. Articles of Association: (1) A company shall frame articles of association to attain the objectives set forth in the memorandum of association and to conduct its business in a well-managed manner.
(2) The articles of association shall state the following matters:
(a) The mode of calling the general meeting of the company and the matters relating to the notice of the meeting;
(b) The procedure of the general meeting;
(c) The number of directors, the provision for alternate directors, if any, and the tenure of directors;
(d) Provisions relating to the record of decisions of the general meeting and the board of directors, and the copy and inspection thereof;
(e) The minimum number of shares, if any, to be held by a person to be appointed as a director of the company;
(f) In the case of a public company, the qualification and number of independent directors;

दफा २०: नियमावली (Articles of Association)
The minimum number of shares, if any, to be held by a person to be appointed as a director of the company;
(f) In the case of a public company, the qualification and number of independent directors;
(g) If any professional person other than a shareholder is to be appointed as a director, the number, tenure, qualification and appointment process of such directors;
(h) The powers and duties of the board of directors and the managing director;
(i) The authority of directors and delegation of authority;
(j) The quorum for the meeting of the board of directors, the notice of the meeting and the procedure of the meeting;
(k) Matters relating to lien on shares;
(l) Different classes of shares and the rights, powers and restrictions inherent in such shares;
(m) Provisions relating to calls on shares and forfeiture of shares;
(n) Provisions relating to the transfer of shares;
(o) Matters relating to the increase or decrease of share capital;
(p) If the company is to buy back its own shares, such matter;
(q) Appointment of the company secretary;
(r) Provisions relating to the remuneration, allowances and facilities of directors;

दफा २०: नियमावली (Articles of Association)
capital;
(p) If the company is to buy back its own shares, such matter;
(q) Appointment of the company secretary;
(r) Provisions relating to the remuneration, allowances and facilities of directors;
(s) Use of the company's seal, if it is to be used in its transactions;
(t) Accounts, books of account and audit of the company;
(u) Provisions relating to the raising of loans or debentures;
(v) Matters relating to the merger of the company;
(w) If the prevailing law requires any matter to be disclosed in the articles of association of a company carrying on any particular business, such matter;
(x) Other necessary matters to be disclosed in the articles of association.
(3) Any provision contained in the articles of association, including any provision relating to the protection of a director or officer of the company, which is inconsistent with this Act and the memorandum of association, shall be void to the extent of such inconsistency.
(4) The format of the articles of association shall be as prescribed.

दफा २१: प्रबन्धपत्र वा नियमावलीमा संशोधन (Amendment of memorandum of association or articles of association)
apply to the Office for prior approval along with the prescribed fee, and if the Office gives approval to amend the name as per the application so received, the name of the company shall be amended.
(4) If a shareholder of a public company is not satisfied with the amendment made to the objectives of the company, he/she may, stating the reasons therefor, apply to the Court to have such amendment declared invalid, upon fulfilling the following conditions:
(a) The application shall be filed by a shareholder or shareholders holding at least five percent of the paid-up capital of the company, other than the shareholders who consented to or voted for the amendment or change;
(b) The application shall be filed within twenty-one days after the date on which the resolution to amend the objectives of the company was passed;
(c) Where an application is to be filed on behalf of one or more shareholders entitled to file an application, the person authorized in writing for that purpose shall file the application.

दफा २१: प्रबन्धपत्र वा नियमावलीमा संशोधन (Amendment of memorandum of association or articles of association)
the Court may issue an appropriate order by specifying the following terms and conditions:
(a) To declare the amendment made to the objectives of the company as valid or invalid, in whole or in part;
(b) To cause the company to purchase the shares and other rights held by the shareholders who filed the application pursuant to sub-section (4) due to disagreement with the change in the main objectives of the company, at a fair price;
(c) While purchasing shares pursuant to clause (b), the purchase shall be made from the amount mentioned in sub-section (2) of Section 61, and in the case of a company which does not have such amount, to issue an order to reduce the capital of the company in such a way that the company passes a special resolution and the share capital is deemed to have been reduced to the extent of the shares so purchased, and where such order is issued, the company shall amend its memorandum of association and articles of association subject to the provisions of this Act.

दफा २९: प्रिमियम मूल्यको शेयर जारी गर्न सकिने (Issue of shares at premium)
ssue of securities pursuant to the prevailing law relating to securities may issue shares at a premium with the approval of the general meeting in a situation where its assets exceed its liabilities.
(2) Where shares are sold at a premium pursuant to sub-section (1), the amount exceeding the face value out of the proceeds shall be deposited into a premium account to be opened for that purpose.
(3) The company may use the amount in the account pursuant to sub-section (2) for the following purposes:
(a) To allot and issue fully paid-up bonus shares to the shareholders out of the unissued share capital;
(b) To provide for the premium payable on the redemption of any redeemable preference shares;
(c) To write off the preliminary expenses of the company;
(d) To bear or reimburse the expenses incurred or commission or discount paid in connection with the issuance of shares of the company.
(4) While seeking approval of the Office to issue shares at a premium pursuant to sub-section (1), audited financial statements for three years shall be provided to the Office.

दफा ३०: फरक अधिकार भएका शेयर र त्यस्ता शेयरधनीको अधिकार (Shares with differential rights and rights of such shareholders)
the rights of the shareholders of the concerned class would be prejudicial to the applicant shareholders, the Court may cancel the decision made to vary the rights of the shareholders of that class.
(6) The board of directors shall submit a resolution relating to the variation of the rights of the shareholders of any particular class pursuant to sub-section (2) to the general meeting of the shareholders of the concerned class, and such resolution shall be passed as a special resolution by the general meeting.
(7) Notwithstanding anything contained elsewhere in this Section, while privatizing a company with full or partial ownership of the Government of Nepal in the capacity of a shareholder according to the prevailing law relating to privatization, the Government of Nepal may have a special voting right as provided in the articles of association while making a decision on the following matters so long as the investment of the Government of Nepal remains in such company:
(a) While deciding on a resolution to alienate rights pursuant to clause (a) of sub-section (1) of Section 105;
(b) While making a decision relating to the voluntary liquidation of the company;

दफा ३०: फरक अधिकार भएका शेयर र त्यस्ता शेयरधनीको अधिकार (Shares with differential rights and rights of such shareholders)
pany:
(a) While deciding on a resolution to alienate rights pursuant to clause (a) of sub-section (1) of Section 105;
(b) While making a decision relating to the voluntary liquidation of the company;
(c) While making a decision to merge the company into another company.

दफा ३६: डिबेञ्चर ट्रष्टी र कम्पनीबीच सम्झौता हुनु पर्ने (Agreement to be entered into between debenture trustee and company)
गर्न गराउन सक्नेछ ।
(५) यस दफा बमोजिम डिबेञ्चर ट्रष्टी र कम्पनीको बीचमा सम्झौता भइसकेपछि त्यस्तो कम्पनीले थप डिबेञ्चर उठाउने भएमा डिबेञ्चर ट्रष्टीको स्वीकृति लिनु पर्नेछ ।

**English Translation:**

36. Agreement to be entered into between debenture trustee and company: (1) In respect of debentures to be raised by any company, an agreement shall be entered into between the company issuing debentures and the debenture trustee acting as a trustee for the protection of the interests of the debenture-holders.
(2) While entering into an agreement pursuant to sub-section (1), the following matters shall be disclosed in such agreement:
(a) That the debenture trustee may make or cause to be made valuation of the assets, project analysis or management analysis of the company;
(b) The time for payment of the principal and interest of the debentures purchased by the debenture-holders, the interest rate, the procedure for payment of principal and interest, and matters relating to the conversion of debentures into shares, if any;
(c) Matters relating to the rights of other creditors in the assets of the company and the provisions made in respect of liabilities to arise in the future;

दफा ३६: डिबेञ्चर ट्रष्टी र कम्पनीबीच सम्झौता हुनु पर्ने (Agreement to be entered into between debenture trustee and company)
version of debentures into shares, if any;
(c) Matters relating to the rights of other creditors in the assets of the company and the provisions made in respect of liabilities to arise in the future;
(d) That if the terms mentioned in the agreement are violated or not fulfilled, or if the financial transactions of the company are to be taken under control for any other reasonable reason, or if the security according to the agreement is to be taken into possession, the debenture trustee may take possession of the assets or property of such company or the property taken by the debenture trustee as security, or keep the security itself or sell it through auction or other appropriate manner;
(e) Matters relating to the procedure for payment of service fees and other direct expenses of the debenture trustee by the company;
(f) That the debenture trustee shall not bear responsibility for any loss or damage caused to the company or the debenture-holders while acting in the capacity of a debenture trustee;

दफा ३६: डिबेञ्चर ट्रष्टी र कम्पनीबीच सम्झौता हुनु पर्ने (Agreement to be entered into between debenture trustee and company)
by the company;
(f) That the debenture trustee shall not bear responsibility for any loss or damage caused to the company or the debenture-holders while acting in the capacity of a debenture trustee;
(g) The legal actions that the debenture trustee may take on behalf of the debenture-holders and the exercise of the rights of the debenture-holders in the event of the dissolution of the company;
(h) Other necessary matters relating to the protection of the interests of the debenture-holders.
(3) The debenture trustee may take the assets of the company as security for the protection of the interests of the debenture-holders and have such security transferred to its name according to the prevailing law.
(4) Before taking security pursuant to sub-section (3), the debenture trustee may, if it deems necessary, make or cause to be made valuation of the property or assets to be taken as security and project analysis or management analysis of the company.
(5) After an agreement has been entered into between the debenture trustee and the company pursuant to this Section, the company shall obtain the approval of the debenture trustee if it is to raise further debentures.

दफा ३७: डिबेञ्चर ट्रष्टीले जाँचबुझ गर्न र विवरण माग गर्न सक्ने (Debenture trustee may inquire and call for details)
िति छ वा छैन,
(घ) कम्पनीका अन्य साहू तथा दायित्वहरु सम्बन्धी विषय,
(ङ) कम्पनीको वासलात तथा लेखापरीक्षकको प्रतिवेदन,
(च) डिबेञ्चर ट्रष्टीले उपयुक्त ठानेको अन्य आवश्यक विषय ।

**English Translation:**

37. Debenture trustee may inquire and call for details: Before entering into an agreement with a company to act as a debenture trustee, the debenture trustee may make necessary inquiries and take or call for details, notices or information on the following matters, and if so called for, the concerned company shall provide the same:
(a) Whether or not there is a provision in the memorandum of association or articles of association of the company to raise loans or debentures, and if there is such a provision, whether or not the board of directors of the company has the power to make a decision to raise debentures;
(b) Whether or not there is a provision to raise debentures through a debenture trustee according to the memorandum of association or articles of association of the company;
(c) Whether or not the existing assets of the company are sufficient to cover the value of the debentures to be raised;
(d) Matters relating to other creditors and liabilities of the company;

दफा ३७: डिबेञ्चर ट्रष्टीले जाँचबुझ गर्न र विवरण माग गर्न सक्ने (Debenture trustee may inquire and call for details)
ompany;
(c) Whether or not the existing assets of the company are sufficient to cover the value of the debentures to be raised;
(d) Matters relating to other creditors and liabilities of the company;
(e) The balance sheet and audit report of the company;
(f) Other necessary matters deemed appropriate by the debenture trustee.

दफा ४६: शेयरधनी र डिबेञ्चरवालाको दर्ता किताब (Register of shareholders and debenture-holders)
ालक, पदामधकारी तथा कमनचारीलाई दफा १६० मा उम्ल्लम्िि दण्ड जररबानाका अमिररक्त झुट्टा अमभलेि राम्िएको कारणबाट पुग्न गएको हामन नोवसानी समेि सम्बम्न्धि पक्ष ले भराई मलन पाउनेछ ।

**English Translation:**

46. Register of shareholders and debenture-holders: (1) Every company shall maintain a register of shareholders and a register of debenture-holders in the prescribed format at its registered office.
(2) The register of shareholders pursuant to sub-section (1) shall state the following matters in respect of each shareholder according to the serial number of shares:
(a) The full name and address of the shareholder;
(b) The number of shares held by the shareholder;
(c) The total amount paid by the shareholder for the shares and the amount remaining to be paid;
(d) The date on which his/her name was entered as a shareholder;
(e) The date on which his/her name was removed;
(f) If any person is nominated to have a right in the shares after the death of the shareholder, the name and address of such person.
(3) The register of debenture-holders pursuant to sub-section (1) shall state the following matters in respect of each debenture-holder according to the serial number of debentures:

दफा ४६: शेयरधनी र डिबेञ्चरवालाको दर्ता किताब (Register of shareholders and debenture-holders)
s of such person.
(3) The register of debenture-holders pursuant to sub-section (1) shall state the following matters in respect of each debenture-holder according to the serial number of debentures:
(a) The full name and address of the debenture-holder;
(b) The number of debentures held by the debenture-holder;
(c) The total amount paid by the debenture-holder for the debentures and the amount remaining to be paid;
(d) The date on which his/her name was entered as a debenture-holder;
(e) The date on which his/her name was removed;
(f) If any person is nominated to have a right in the debentures after the death of the debenture-holder, the name and address of such person.
(4) If a shareholder or debenture-holder of a company wishes to inspect the register maintained pursuant to sub-section (1), the company shall allow such inspection.

दफा ५१: शेयर, डिबेञ्चर र ऋणको लगि (Records of shares, debentures and loans)
म् पनीले दफा ७८ बमोम्जम पेश गनुन पने प्र मििेदनमा उपदफा (२) बमोम्जमका हििरणहरु समेि उल् लेि गरेको भए त् यस्िो कम् पनीले यस दफा बमोम्जम छुट्टै लगि कायानलयमा पठाउनु पने छैन ।

**English Translation:**

51. Records of shares, debentures and loans: (1) Every company shall, twenty-one days before the annual general meeting, prepare and maintain a record of the shareholders and debenture-holders existing for the time being and those whose names have been removed, up to thirty days before the annual general meeting.
(2) The record pursuant to sub-section (1) shall, in addition to other matters, disclose the following:
(a) The authorized capital of the company and the number of shares;
(b) The issued share capital of the company;
(c) The paid-up capital of the company;
(d) The amount called on each share;
(e) The total amount of installments collected;
(f) The total amount remaining to be collected;
(g) The total amount paid as brokerage fee on shares or debentures;
(h) Where any shares have been forfeited, the total number of such shares, the reason for and date of forfeiture;

दफा ५१: शेयर, डिबेञ्चर र ऋणको लगि (Records of shares, debentures and loans)
to be collected;
(g) The total amount paid as brokerage fee on shares or debentures;
(h) Where any shares have been forfeited, the total number of such shares, the reason for and date of forfeiture;
(i) The loans taken from banks, financial institutions or any other persons or the guarantees given by the company;
(i1) If investment has been made in the shares or debentures of other companies, the name and registration number of such company and the amount of investment made in the shares or debentures;
(j) The names and addresses of the directors for the time being.
(3) The record pursuant to sub-section (1) shall be signed by at least one director and sent to the Office within thirty days from the date of the annual general meeting of the company, and in the case of a company which does not hold an annual general meeting, within one year from the date of obtaining approval if it carries on a business requiring approval from the concerned body under the prevailing law, or within one year from the date of registration if such approval is not required.

दफा ५६: शेयर पुुँजी हेरफेर गने कम्पनीको अमधकाराः (Power of company to alter share capital)
shareholders of the company shall not have the first right to purchase the following shares to be issued by the company:
(a) Shares to be issued by the company for any consideration other than cash;
(b) Shares issued to any person under any right or facility granted in accordance with the terms of an agreement with the company;
(c) Shares issued under an employee share scheme;
(d) Shares issued in accordance with an agreement between a company and its creditors;
(e) Shares created when a company converts preference shares into ordinary shares or debentures into shares;
(f) Shares issued in accordance with an agreement entered into between the concerned parties in the course of restructuring the management, capital or debt of the company, or in the course of implementing a restructuring program approved under the prevailing law relating to insolvency, or in the course of implementing a program for the merger of one public company into another public company.
(10) A company shall not increase its share capital or issue bonus shares by revaluing the assets of the company, except from the profits earned by the company or from a fund created out of such profits.

दफा ६१: कम्पनीले आफ्नो शेयर आपैmंले खरिद गर्न नहुने (Company not to buy back its own shares)
in the following circumstances:
(a) If the entire amount of shares issued by the company has been paid up;
(b) If the shares issued by a public company have been registered with the Securities Board;
(c) If there is a provision in the articles of association of the concerned company allowing it to buy back its own shares;
(d) If a special resolution has been passed in the general meeting of the concerned company allowing it to buy back its own shares;
(e) If the amount of debt to be paid by the company does not exceed double the ratio of its capital and general reserve fund after the company has bought back its own shares;
Explanation: For the purpose of this clause, "debt amount" means the entire secured and unsecured loan amount taken by the company.
(f) If the amount of its own shares to be purchased by the company does not exceed twenty percent of the total paid-up capital and general reserve fund of the company;
(g) If it is not contrary to the directives issued by the Office from time to time in relation to the buyback of its own shares.

दफा ६१: कम्पनीले आफ्नो शेयर आपैmंले खरिद गर्न नहुने (Company not to buy back its own shares)
of the total paid-up capital and general reserve fund of the company;
(g) If it is not contrary to the directives issued by the Office from time to time in relation to the buyback of its own shares.
(3) The resolution to be placed before the general meeting pursuant to clause (d) of sub-section (2) shall contain the following particulars:
(a) The reason for and necessity of buying back its own shares;
(b) A description of the assessment of the possible impact on the financial position of the concerned company due to the buyback of its own shares;
(c) The type and number of shares proposed to be purchased;
(d) The maximum or minimum amount required to purchase the shares pursuant to clause (c) and its financial source;
(e) The period within which its own shares can be bought back;
(f) The method of purchasing shares;
(g) Other necessary matters prescribed by the Office and required to be disclosed under the prevailing law in relation to the buyback of its own shares.

दफा ६१: कम्पनीले आफ्नो शेयर आपैmंले खरिद गर्न नहुने (Company not to buy back its own shares)
ght back;
(f) The method of purchasing shares;
(g) Other necessary matters prescribed by the Office and required to be disclosed under the prevailing law in relation to the buyback of its own shares.
(4) If a special resolution pursuant to sub-section (3) is passed by the general meeting, the concerned company may buy back its own shares by any of the following means within twelve months from the date of passing of such resolution:
(a) By purchasing through the stock exchange;
(b) By purchasing from the employees the shares allotted to them;
(c) By purchasing proportionately from the existing shareholders.
(5) If a company buys back its own shares pursuant to sub-section (4), it shall inform the Office of the number of shares bought back, the amount paid therefor and other necessary particulars within thirty days from the date of such buyback.
(6) An amount equivalent to the face value of the shares bought back by the company pursuant to sub-section (4) shall be deposited into a separate capital redemption reserve fund to be created for that purpose, and the amount of such fund shall be maintained as paid-up capital.

दफा ६५: अग्राधिकार शेयर (Preference shares)
to ordinary shares;
(b) The percentage of dividends to be received by preference shareholders;
(c) Whether dividends are cumulative or non-cumulative (i.e., distributed only in profit-making years);
(d) Whether or not preference is to be given in refunding the share amount in the event of liquidation of the company;
(e) Whether or not there are voting rights, and if there are voting rights, whether they are only on matters relating to preference shares or also on other matters;
(f) If there are voting rights on other matters pursuant to clause (e), the proportion in which such voting rights are to be exercised;
(g) Whether or not they are convertible into ordinary shares;
(h) Whether the preference share amount is redeemable after a certain period or irredeemable;
(i) Whether the preference shares are to be redeemed with or without a premium.
(4) If any preference shares are issued on the condition of redemption, such shares shall not be redeemable until their full value has been paid up.

दफा ७८: कार्यालयमा प्रतिवेदन पेश गर्नु पर्ने (Report to be submitted to Office)
्चको विवरण,
(ढ) शेयरधनीहरुले बुझिलिन बाँकी रहेको लाभांशको रकम,
(ण) कम्पनीले यस ऐन तथा प्रचलित कानूनको पालना पूर्ण रुपमा गरेको छ भन्ने कुराको उद्घोषण,
(त) अन्य आवश्यक कुरा ।

**English Translation:**

78. Report to be submitted to Office: Every public company shall prepare a report disclosing the following matters and submit it to the Office at least twenty-one days prior to the annual general meeting. Such report shall be approved by the board of directors and certified by the auditor of the company:
(a) The number of shares allotted;
(b) The number of paid-up and unpaid shares among the allotted shares;
(c) The details of the directors, managing directors, auditors, chief executives, managers of the company and the amount of remuneration, allowances and facilities paid to them;
(d) The names of persons or body corporates who have purchased five percent or more of the paid-up capital of the company and the details of shares or debentures held in their names;
(e) The total amount received from the sale of shares and the details of new shares and debentures purchased and issued by the company in the concerned financial year;

दफा ७८: कार्यालयमा प्रतिवेदन पेश गर्नु पर्ने (Report to be submitted to Office)
debentures held in their names;
(e) The total amount received from the sale of shares and the details of new shares and debentures purchased and issued by the company in the concerned financial year;
(f) The amount remaining to be paid by a director or substantial shareholder or his/her close relative to the company;
(g) The amount paid or payable for the sale of shares or any other work;
(h) The amount of principal and interest of loans taken from banks and financial institutions and remaining to be paid;
(i) The amount claimed to be received by the company or to be paid by the company to other persons, or the details of any lawsuit pending in this regard;
(j) The number of employees or workers engaged in the management and other levels of the company;
(k) The number of foreigners engaged in the management and other levels of the company and the remuneration, allowances and facilities paid to them;

दफा ७८: कार्यालयमा प्रतिवेदन पेश गर्नु पर्ने (Report to be submitted to Office)
in the management and other levels of the company;
(k) The number of foreigners engaged in the management and other levels of the company and the remuneration, allowances and facilities paid to them;
(l) If any agreement has been entered into between the company and any foreign body or persons for investment, management or technical services or other matters for a period exceeding one year, the details thereof and the details of dividends, commissions, fees, charges and royalties, etc., paid in the concerned financial year pursuant to such agreement;
(m) The details of the management expenses of the company for one financial year;
(n) The amount of dividends remaining to be received by the shareholders;
(o) A declaration that the company has fully complied with this Act and the prevailing law;
(p) Other necessary matters.

दफा ८१: विवरण नपठाएमा जरिवाना हुने (Penalty for not submitting report)
ers of the following companies who fail to provide the report, notice, information or reply pursuant to Section 51, 78, 80, 120, 131 or 156 within the period mentioned in sub-section (1), as follows:
(a) For a period of up to three months from the expiry of the period, if the company has a paid-up capital of up to two million five hundred thousand rupees, a fine of one thousand rupees; if the company has a paid-up capital of up to ten million rupees, a fine of two thousand rupees; and if the company has a paid-up capital of more than ten million rupees, a fine of five thousand rupees;
(b) For an additional period of up to three months from the date of expiry of the period mentioned in clause (a), if the company has a paid-up capital of up to two million five hundred thousand rupees, a fine of one thousand five hundred rupees; if the company has a paid-up capital of up to ten million rupees, a fine of three thousand rupees; and if the company has a paid-up capital of more than ten million rupees, a fine of seven thousand rupees;

दफा ८१: विवरण नपठाएमा जरिवाना हुने (Penalty for not submitting report)
company has a paid-up capital of up to ten million rupees, a fine of three thousand rupees; and if the company has a paid-up capital of more than ten million rupees, a fine of seven thousand rupees;
(c) For an additional period of up to six months after the expiry of the period mentioned in clause (b), if the company has a paid-up capital of up to two million five hundred thousand rupees, a fine of two thousand five hundred rupees; if the company has a paid-up capital of up to ten million rupees, a fine of five thousand rupees; and if the company has a paid-up capital of more than ten million rupees, a fine of ten thousand rupees;
(d) If the period mentioned in clause (c) has also expired, if the company has a paid-up capital of up to two million five hundred thousand rupees, a fine of five thousand rupees for each year; if the company has a paid-up capital of up to ten million rupees, a fine of ten thousand rupees for each year; and if the company has a paid-up capital of more than ten million rupees, a fine of twenty thousand rupees for each year.

दफा ८३: विशेष प्रस्ताव पेश गर्नु पर्ने (Special resolution to be submitted)
(ज) प्राइभेट कम्पनी पब्लिक कम्पनीमा वा पब्लिक कम्पनी प्राइभेट कम्पनीमा परिणत हुने विषय,
(झ) यस ऐन वा नियमावलीमा कम्पनीले विशेष प्रस्ताव पारित गर्नु पर्ने भनिएको अन्य विषय ।

**English Translation:**

83. Special resolution to be submitted: A special resolution shall be submitted to the general meeting of the company for making decisions on the following matters:
(a) Matters relating to increasing the authorized capital of the company;
(b) Matters relating to reducing or altering the share capital of the company;
(c) Matters relating to changing the name or main objectives of the company;
(d) Matters relating to the merger of one company into another company;
(e) Matters relating to the issue of bonus shares;
(f) Matters relating to the buyback of its own shares by the company;
(g) Matters relating to the sale of shares at a discount;
(h) Matters relating to the conversion of a private company into a public company or a public company into a private company;
(i) Other matters for which the company is required to pass a special resolution in this Act or the articles of association.

दफा ८४: शेयरधनीहरुलाई संक्षिप्त आर्थिक विवरण पठाउने व्यवस्था (Provision for sending abridged financial statements to shareholders)
Provided, however, that when sending the notice of the annual general meeting, an abridged annual financial statement prepared pursuant to sub-sections (2) and (3) shall be sent to each shareholder.
(2) The abridged financial statement to be sent pursuant to the proviso to sub-section (1) shall be prepared on the basis of the company's annual financial statements and directors' report. The format of such statement shall be as prescribed by the Office on the basis of the recommendation of the body designated to determine accounting standards according to the prevailing law.
(3) The abridged annual financial statement shall, in addition to other matters, disclose the following:
(a) The fact that the abridged annual financial statement is only a summary of the company's annual financial statements and directors' report;
(b) The auditor's opinion as to whether or not the abridged annual financial statement is in conformity with the company's annual financial statements and directors' report, and whether or not such statement is in conformity with the format prescribed under this Section;

दफा ८४: शेयरधनीहरुलाई संक्षिप्त आर्थिक विवरण पठाउने व्यवस्था (Provision for sending abridged financial statements to shareholders)
cial statement is in conformity with the company's annual financial statements and directors' report, and whether or not such statement is in conformity with the format prescribed under this Section;
(c) Whether or not the auditor has made any qualification in respect of the company's annual financial statements, and if any qualification has been made, the full details of such qualification and the materials required to understand such qualification;
(d) The full details relating to the auditor's report if the auditor has stated in his/her report that the company's accounts and accounting records are incomplete or that the company's accounts do not conform to the records and statements maintained by the company or that the information and explanations called for have not been received.
(4) Instead of sending the abridged annual financial statement to the personal address of the shareholders pursuant to sub-section (1), the company may publish it in a national level daily newspaper at least twice at the time of publishing the notice of the meeting on that matter.

दफा ८९: सञ्चालकको पदमा नियुक्त हुन वा बहाल रहन नसक्ने अवस्था (Circumstances in which a person cannot be appointed or remain in office as director)
यम रहेको भएमा ।
(४) कुनै व्यक्तिलाई सञ्चालकको पदमा नियुक्त हुन वा बहाल रहन अयोग्य ठहर्याउनु अघि कम्पनीले निजलाई सो कुराको सूचना दिई सफाई पेश गर्ने मनासिब मौका दिनु पर्नेछ ।

**English Translation:**

89. Circumstances in which a person cannot be appointed or remain in office as director: (1) None of the following persons shall be appointed as a director:
(a) In the case of a public company, a person who has not attained twenty-one years of age;
(b) A person of unsound mind or a lunatic;
(c) A person who has been declared insolvent and a period of five years has not elapsed since such declaration;
(d) A person who has been punished for corruption or any other offense involving moral turpitude;
Provided, however, that in the case of a private company, a period of three years has not elapsed since the date of payment of such punishment;
(e) A person who has been convicted of theft, fraud, forgery or unauthorized misappropriation or misuse of property entrusted to him/her and a period of three years has not elapsed since the date of payment of such punishment;
(f) A person who has any personal interest in the business of the concerned company or in any contract or transaction;

दफा ८९: सञ्चालकको पदमा नियुक्त हुन वा बहाल रहन नसक्ने अवस्था (Circumstances in which a person cannot be appointed or remain in office as director)
iod of three years has not elapsed since the date of payment of such punishment;
(f) A person who has any personal interest in the business of the concerned company or in any contract or transaction;
(g) A person who is serving as a director, substantial shareholder, employee, auditor or advisor of another company having similar objectives, or who has any personal interest in such company;
Provided, however, that such person of a private company may be a director in another private company having similar objectives.
(h) A shareholder who has been found to be liable to pay any amount to the concerned company;
(i) In the case of a person punished under Section 160, a period of one year has not elapsed since the date of punishment, or in the case of a person punished under Section 161, a period of six months has not elapsed since the date of punishment;
(j) In the case of a company carrying on any particular business, a person who does not possess the qualifications prescribed by the prevailing law or who has any disqualification prescribed by such law;

दफा ८९: सञ्चालकको पदमा नियुक्त हुन वा बहाल रहन नसक्ने अवस्था (Circumstances in which a person cannot be appointed or remain in office as director)
In the case of a company carrying on any particular business, a person who does not possess the qualifications prescribed by the prevailing law or who has any disqualification prescribed by such law;
(k) A person who is a director of a company that has not submitted the reports and statements required to be submitted to the Office under this Act for three consecutive financial years;
(k1) A person who has outstanding fine amount to be paid pursuant to sub-section (2) of Section 81;
(l) A person who is serving as a director of another listed company and receives remuneration or any facility other than meeting allowance and actual expenses incurred for coming, going and staying at the meeting place.
(2) None of the following persons shall be appointed as an independent director:
(a) A person as mentioned in sub-section (1);
(b) A shareholder of the concerned company;

दफा ८९: सञ्चालकको पदमा नियुक्त हुन वा बहाल रहन नसक्ने अवस्था (Circumstances in which a person cannot be appointed or remain in office as director)
taying at the meeting place.
(2) None of the following persons shall be appointed as an independent director:
(a) A person as mentioned in sub-section (1);
(b) A shareholder of the concerned company;
(c) A person who has not obtained at least a graduate degree in a subject related to the business of the concerned company and has at least ten years of experience in the relevant field or in company management, or who has not obtained at least a graduate degree in economics, finance, management, accounting, statistics, commerce, business administration or law and has at least ten years of experience in the relevant field;
(d) A person who has not completed three years since his/her retirement from the post of officer, auditor or employee of the concerned company;
(e) A close relative of an officer of the concerned company;
(f) The auditor of the concerned company or his/her partner.
(3) No person shall remain in office as a director in the following circumstances:
(a) If he/she is in a circumstance where he/she cannot be appointed as a director as mentioned in sub-section (1) or (2);
(b) If the general meeting passes a resolution to remove him/her from the office of director;

दफा ८९: सञ्चालकको पदमा नियुक्त हुन वा बहाल रहन नसक्ने अवस्था (Circumstances in which a person cannot be appointed or remain in office as director)
in a circumstance where he/she cannot be appointed as a director as mentioned in sub-section (1) or (2);
(b) If the general meeting passes a resolution to remove him/her from the office of director;
(c) If the resignation submitted by the director from his/her office is approved by the board of directors;
(d) If it is proved by the Court that he/she has committed dishonesty or bad faith in the affairs of the company;
(e) If it is proved by the Court that the director has committed any act prohibited by this Act or has failed to perform any act required by this Act;
(f) If he/she has been blacklisted by an authorized body for non-payment of a loan from a bank or financial institution under the prevailing law and the period of blacklisting is still in effect.
(4) Before declaring any person ineligible to be appointed or to remain in office as a director, the company shall give him/her notice thereof and a reasonable opportunity to present his/her defense.

दफा ९३: सञ्चालकको संलग्नता रहेको कम्पनीसँगको कारोबार (Transactions with company in which director has interest)
pay compensation for the same.
(3) Notwithstanding anything contained elsewhere in this Section, the provisions of sub-section (1) shall not apply in respect of in-kind property acquired as follows:
(a) When a holding company acquires such property from its wholly-owned subsidiary company;
(b) When a wholly-owned subsidiary company of a holding company acquires such property from another wholly-owned subsidiary company of the same holding company;
(c) When carrying out transactions at prevailing market prices in the ordinary course of business of the company.

दफा ९४: सञ्चालकले शेयर बारेमा जानकारी गराउनु पर्ने (Directors to provide information about shares)
in the shares or debentures of the company in which he/she is a director or its subsidiary or holding company or any other subsidiary company of the holding company, or if his/her right is to cease;
(b) If he/she enters into any agreement to sell the shares or debentures mentioned in clause (a) registered in his/her name;
(c) If the company in which he/she is a director transfers to anyone else the right granted to purchase the shares or debentures of such company;
(d) If a subsidiary or holding company of the company in which he/she is a director, or a subsidiary company of such company or any other subsidiary company of the holding company, grants the right to purchase the shares or debentures of such company;
(e) If he/she transfers to anyone else the right to purchase the shares or debentures of the company mentioned in clause (d).
(3) While sending information to the company pursuant to sub-section (2), the number, amount and class of shares or debentures shall be clearly stated.
(4) The company shall maintain a separate register for recording the information received pursuant to sub-sections (2) and (3).

दफा ९५: सञ्चालक समितिको अधिकार र कर्तव्य (Powers and duties of Board of Directors)
company may recover from a director or representative any loss or damage caused to the company by any act done by him/her in the capacity of a director or representative exceeding his/her authority.
(5) If any person knowingly or having reason to believe that a director or representative pursuant to sub-section (3) is about to carry out any transaction for his/her personal benefit or to cause loss or damage to the company, enters into any transaction with such director or representative, such person shall not be entitled to make any claim against the company in respect of such transaction.
(6) Notwithstanding anything contained in sub-section (3), the board of directors shall not be entitled to delegate the following powers conferred on the company, and such powers shall be exercised only in accordance with the decisions passed by the meeting of the board of directors:
(a) The power to call for payment of amounts remaining to be paid by shareholders for shares;
(b) The power to issue debentures;
(c) The power to take loans or borrowings by means other than debentures;
(d) The power to invest the amount in the company's fund;
(e) The power to grant loans.

दफा ९५: सञ्चालक समितिको अधिकार र कर्तव्य (Powers and duties of Board of Directors)
s;
(b) The power to issue debentures;
(c) The power to take loans or borrowings by means other than debentures;
(d) The power to invest the amount in the company's fund;
(e) The power to grant loans.
(7) The provisions of clause (e) of sub-section (6) shall not apply in the case of loans granted and deposits received by banking and financial companies in the ordinary course of business.
(8) If the board of directors deems it necessary to constitute a sub-committee to carry out any particular work, it may constitute one or more sub-committees as required and cause such work to be carried out.

दफा १०९: वार्षिक आर्थिक विवरण र सञ्चालक समितिको प्रतिवेदन तयार गर्नु पर्ने (Annual financial statements and directors' report to be prepared)
nths of the end of the financial year:
(a) Balance sheet as of the last date of the financial year;
(b) Profit and loss account for the financial year;
(c) Cash flow statement for the financial year.
(2) The annual financial statements to be prepared pursuant to sub-section (1) shall show the true and fair view of the company's transactions up to the end of the concerned financial year and shall also include the profit and loss account and cash flow statement for that financial year. Such financial statements shall be prepared in the format prescribed by the prevailing law.
(3) The annual financial statements pursuant to sub-section (1) shall be approved by the board of directors and audited.
(4) The board of directors of every public company or every private company with a paid-up capital of ten million rupees or more or with an annual turnover of one hundred million rupees or more shall, in addition to the annual financial statements to be prepared pursuant to sub-section (1), also prepare a separate report of the board of directors within the same period, disclosing the following particulars:
(a) Overview of the transactions of the previous year;

दफा १०९: वार्षिक आर्थिक विवरण र सञ्चालक समितिको प्रतिवेदन तयार गर्नु पर्ने (Annual financial statements and directors' report to be prepared)
suant to sub-section (1), also prepare a separate report of the board of directors within the same period, disclosing the following particulars:
(a) Overview of the transactions of the previous year;
(b) The impact, if any, of national and international circumstances on the company's transactions;
(c) The opinion of the board of directors regarding the achievements of the current year up to the date of preparation of the report and matters to be done in the future;
(d) Industrial or business relations of the company;
(e) Changes in the board of directors and the reasons therefor;
(f) Key matters affecting the transactions;
(g) The response of the board of directors to any qualification mentioned in the audit report;
(h) The amount recommended for dividend distribution;
(i) If shares have been forfeited, the number of shares forfeited, their face value, the total amount received by the company for such shares before forfeiture, and the amount received by the company from the sale of such shares after forfeiture, and if any amount has been refunded for the forfeited shares, the details thereof;

दफा १०९: वार्षिक आर्थिक विवरण र सञ्चालक समितिको प्रतिवेदन तयार गर्नु पर्ने (Annual financial statements and directors' report to be prepared)
such shares before forfeiture, and the amount received by the company from the sale of such shares after forfeiture, and if any amount has been refunded for the forfeited shares, the details thereof;
(j) Review of the progress of the transactions of the company and its subsidiary company in the previous financial year and the position at the end of that financial year;
(k) Major transactions completed by the company and its subsidiary company in the financial year and any significant changes in the company's transactions during that period;
(l) Information provided by the substantial shareholders of the company to the company in the previous financial year;
(m) Details of share ownership of the directors and officers of the company in the previous financial year and information received by the company from them regarding their involvement in the company's share transactions, if any;
(n) Details of information provided regarding the personal interest of any director and his/her close relative in agreements related to the company in the previous financial year;

दफा १०९: वार्षिक आर्थिक विवरण र सञ्चालक समितिको प्रतिवेदन तयार गर्नु पर्ने (Annual financial statements and directors' report to be prepared)
ansactions, if any;
(n) Details of information provided regarding the personal interest of any director and his/her close relative in agreements related to the company in the previous financial year;
(o) If the company has bought back its own shares, the reason for such buyback, the number and face value of such shares, and the amount paid by the company for such buyback;
(p) Whether or not there is an internal control system, and if there is, a detailed description thereof;
(q) Details of the total management expenses for the previous financial year;
(r) Names of the members of the audit committee, their remuneration, allowances and facilities received, details of the work done by the committee and details of any recommendations made by the committee;
(s) If any amount is due to the company from a director, managing director, chief executive, substantial shareholder of the company or his/her close relative or a firm, company or body corporate in which he/she is involved, such matter;
(t) The amount of remuneration, allowances and facilities paid to directors, managing directors, chief executives and officers;

दफा १०९: वार्षिक आर्थिक विवरण र सञ्चालक समितिको प्रतिवेदन तयार गर्नु पर्ने (Annual financial statements and directors' report to be prepared)
rm, company or body corporate in which he/she is involved, such matter;
(t) The amount of remuneration, allowances and facilities paid to directors, managing directors, chief executives and officers;
(u) The amount of dividends remaining to be received by the shareholders;
(v) Details of purchase or sale of assets pursuant to Section 141;
(w) Details of transactions between related companies pursuant to Section 175;
(x) Any other matter required to be disclosed in the directors' report pursuant to this Act and the prevailing law;
(y) Other necessary matters.
(5) While preparing the annual financial statements pursuant to sub-section (1), in the case of the year of incorporation of the company, it shall include the period from the date of incorporation to the end of that financial year, and in subsequent years, it shall also include the accounts of the previous financial year.
(6) The annual financial statements prepared pursuant to this Section shall be kept open for inspection by any shareholder who wishes to inspect them.

दफा ११२: लेखापरीक्षकमा नियुक्त हुन नसक्ने (Ineligibility for appointment as auditor)
अयोग्य भएमा वा कम्पनीको लेखापरीक्षक नियुक्त हुन वा कायम रहन नसक्ने स्थिति उत्पन्न भएमा निजले लेखापरीक्षण गर्नु पर्ने वा गरिरहेको काम तत्काल रोकी सो कुराको जानकारी लिखित रुपमा कम्पनीलाई दिनु पर्नेछ ।
(४) यस दफाको प्रतिकूल हुने गरी नियुक्त भएको लेखापरीक्षकले गरेको लेखापरीक्षण मान्य हुने छैन ।

**English Translation:**

112. Ineligibility for appointment as auditor: (1) The following persons or a firm or company in which such persons are partners shall not be appointed as auditor, and if already appointed, shall not remain in office:
(a) A director of the company, a consultant appointed to receive regular remuneration or cash facilities, a person or employee or worker in the management group of the company, or a partner of any of them, or an employee of any such partner, or a close relative of a director or partner among them, or his/her employee;
(b) A debtor who has taken a loan from the company in any manner, or a person who has not paid any amount due to the company within the stipulated period, or a close relative of such person;
(c) A person who has been punished for an offense related to audit and a period of three years has not elapsed since the payment of such punishment;

दफा ११२: लेखापरीक्षकमा नियुक्त हुन नसक्ने (Ineligibility for appointment as auditor)
ulated period, or a close relative of such person;
(c) A person who has been punished for an offense related to audit and a period of three years has not elapsed since the payment of such punishment;
(d) A person who has been declared insolvent;
(e) A substantial shareholder of the company or a shareholder holding one percent or more of the paid-up capital of the company or his/her close relative;
(f) A person who has been punished for corruption, fraud or a criminal offense involving moral turpitude and a period of five years has not elapsed since the payment of such punishment;
(g) A person as mentioned in sub-section (3) of Section 111;
(h) In the case of a public company, a person working full-time or part-time in any government or fully or partially owned or controlled institution of the Government of Nepal or any other company, or his/her partner, or a person working as an employee of such partner, or a person authorized to sign any instrument or report prepared on behalf of the management of the company;
(i) A limited liability company or body corporate;

दफा ११५: लेखापरीक्षकको काम र कर्तव्य (Functions and duties of auditor)
sary for the completion of the audit were available;
(b) Whether or not the company has maintained accounts in accordance with this Act so as to clearly reflect the true position of its transactions;
(c) Whether or not the balance sheet, profit and loss account and cash flow statement received have been prepared in accordance with the accounting standards determined under the prevailing law, and whether or not such statements are in conformity with the accounts maintained by the company;
(d) Based on the explanations and information provided during the audit, whether or not the balance sheet presented with the auditor's opinion, and the profit and loss account and cash flow statement for the year ended on that date, respectively, give a true and fair view of the company's financial position, profit or loss and cash flow;
(e) If any director, representative or employee has acted against the law, or misappropriated the company's assets, or caused loss or damage to the company, such matter;
(f) Whether or not any fraud relating to accounts has been committed in the company;
(g) Any suggestions, if any.

दफा १३१: लिक्विडेटरको अधिकार र कर्तव्य (Powers and duties of liquidator)
हरु लाई गररएको हििरणहरुका सम्बन्धमा प्र मििेदन ियार गरी लेिापरीक्ष कको प्र मििेदनसहहि कम्पनी िारेजी भएको व् यहोरा प्र माम्णि गरी त् यस्िो प्र मििेदन कायानलय समक्ष पेश गने ।

**English Translation:**

131. Powers and duties of liquidator: (1) The liquidator appointed under this Act may exercise all the powers and perform all the duties to be exercised and performed by a liquidator under the prevailing law relating to insolvency, mutatis mutandis.
(2) Without prejudice to the generality of sub-section (1), it shall be the duty of the liquidator to perform the following acts and proceedings:
(a) To prepare an account and statement of income and expenditure relating to the liquidation of the company every six months after the appointment of the liquidator and submit it to the Office;
(b) To inform the shareholders of the company about the progress of the liquidation proceedings every six months after the appointment of the liquidator;
(c) To recover all properties to be received or amounts to be recovered on behalf of the company and pay off the debts and other liabilities of all the creditors of the company;

दफा १३१: लिक्विडेटरको अधिकार र कर्तव्य (Powers and duties of liquidator)
nt of the liquidator;
(c) To recover all properties to be received or amounts to be recovered on behalf of the company and pay off the debts and other liabilities of all the creditors of the company;
(d) After the completion of the act pursuant to clause (c), to call a general meeting and submit a proposed report and statement regarding the distribution of the remaining property of the company to the shareholders;
(e) If the statement pursuant to clause (d) is approved by shareholders holding at least seventy-five percent of the paid-up share capital, to make payments to the shareholders accordingly;
(f) After the completion of the liquidation proceedings, to prepare a report regarding the properties recovered on behalf of the company, payments made to creditors, and distributions made to shareholders, and submit such report to the Office, certifying the liquidation of the company along with the auditor's report.

दफा १३९: शेयरधनीहरुको हक हितविरुद्ध भएको काम कारबाहीको उपचार (Remedy for acts done against rights and interests of shareholders)
and controlling the company has acted or is about to act in bad faith or with unfair discrimination in contravention of the memorandum of association, articles of association or unanimous agreement.
(3) If an application pursuant to sub-section (1) is received, the Court may, after inquiring with the concerned company, director or officer, issue such order in the name of the company as it deems appropriate to provide a remedy, if the claim mentioned in the application appears to be well-founded.
(4) While issuing an order pursuant to sub-section (3), without prejudice to the generality of that sub-section, and notwithstanding anything contained in the memorandum of association, articles of association or unanimous agreement, the Court may also issue the following orders:
(a) To stop the acts and proceedings prejudicial to the rights and interests of any or all shareholders and to conduct the transactions of the company duly in the future;
(b) To stop any act or proceeding being done or about to be done by the company, or to cause the company to do any act which it has not done or is not doing;

दफा १३९: शेयरधनीहरुको हक हितविरुद्ध भएको काम कारबाहीको उपचार (Remedy for acts done against rights and interests of shareholders)
ctions of the company duly in the future;
(b) To stop any act or proceeding being done or about to be done by the company, or to cause the company to do any act which it has not done or is not doing;
(c) To cause a civil lawsuit to be filed against anyone on behalf of the company as directed by the Court;
(d) To cause the share capital of the company to be reduced by fulfilling the procedure of this Act and to purchase the shares of any shareholder and refund the amount;
(e) To cause the company or the person making such discrimination to pay compensation for the loss or damage caused to any shareholder due to discrimination against him/her;
(f) To liquidate the company;
(g) To cause the shares held in the name of any shareholder of the company to be purchased by another shareholder of the company or by the company itself;
(h) To cause the director or officer causing loss or damage to the company or its shareholders to pay compensation for the loss or damage;

दफा १३९: शेयरधनीहरुको हक हितविरुद्ध भएको काम कारबाहीको उपचार (Remedy for acts done against rights and interests of shareholders)
another shareholder of the company or by the company itself;
(h) To cause the director or officer causing loss or damage to the company or its shareholders to pay compensation for the loss or damage;
(i) If the company itself is to purchase the shares, to issue an order to reduce the share capital of such company, deeming it as if the share capital has been reduced by passing a special resolution in respect of the reduction of share capital by such company, and to issue other appropriate orders, including making necessary amendments if the memorandum of association or articles of association of the company need to be amended due to such reason.

दफा १४१: सम्पत्तिको प्राप्ति वा बिक्री (Acquisition or sale of property)
(b) If the income from the property to be sold or sold exceeds fifteen percent of the consolidated income of the company before paying tax as mentioned in the latest audited accounts of the company.
(2) While providing information to the Office pursuant to sub-section (1), the following matters shall be disclosed, and if such matters are also applicable in respect of the transactions of the company, such matters shall also be shown in the report of the board of directors:
(a) The date of the transaction and the parties involved in the transaction;
(b) Details regarding the nature of the property, and if such property includes, wholly or partly, shares issued by any other company, the name of the company issuing such shares and the nature of the business transactions carried on by such company;
(c) The amount of the transaction and other terms of the transaction;
(d) The bases adopted for the valuation of the property while acquiring or selling the property;
(e) If any property has been sold, whether the amount received from the sale of the property is more or less than the value shown in the records of such property.

दफा १४३: कागजात समावेश गर्नु पर्ने (Documents to be included)
(३) कुनै कारणिश मुख् य कम्पनीको सञ्चालक समममिले उपदफा (१) को िण्ड (ि) र उपदफा (२) मा उम्ल्लम्िि जानकारी हामसल गनन नसकेमा मुख् य कम्पनीको िासलािमा सो कुराको मलम्िि प्र मििेदन समािेश गरेको हुनु पनेछ ।
(४) उपदफा (१) को िण्ड (ग) बमोम्जमको हििरणमा सहायक कम्पनीको अचल जायजेथा मधिो रािी मलएको ऋण िा ित्काल कायम रहेको दाहयत्ि पुरा गननबाहेक अरु कुनै कामको लामग मलएको ऋणसमेि देिाउनु पनेछ ।

**English Translation:**

143. Documents to be included: (1) A holding company shall include the following documents of its subsidiary company in its balance sheet:
(a) A copy of the annual accounts of the subsidiary company for the immediately preceding financial year and the report of the board of directors of such company for that period;
(b) The auditor's report;
(c) A statement of the holding company's investment in the subsidiary company at the end of the financial year;
(d) If the financial years of the holding company and the subsidiary company are different, any change in the holding company's right over the subsidiary company during such different period.

दफा १४५: सर्वसम्मति सम्झौता (Unanimous agreement)
स्थापन , शेयरधनीलाई प्र ाप्त मिामधकार िा अन्य कुनै हिशेष सहुमलयि, अमधकार िा शेयरधनीबीचको आपसी सम्बन्ध सम्बन्धी हिषय ।
(२) सम्झौिाका सबै पक्षहरुको मलम्िि सहममिबाट सिनसम्मि सम्झौिामा संशोधन हुन सवनेछ ।
(३) सिनसम्मि सम्झौिा सम्पन्न भइसकेपमछ देहाय बमोम्जम गरी शेयर प्र ाप्त गने शेयरधनीले सो सम्झौिामा सहममि जनाएको र सोको पक्ष भएको मामननेछाः–
(क) दान बकसबाट शेयर पाएको भएमा,
(ि) अन्य कुनै ििरबाट शेयर प्र ाप्त गरेकोमा सो शेयर प्र ाप्त गरेका बिि त् यस्िो सम्झौिा रहेको जानकारी भएमा ।

**English Translation:**

145. Unanimous agreement: (1) Unless otherwise provided in this Act, the unanimous agreement of a private company may provide for the following matters:
(a) Management, business and transactions of the company;
(b) Any restrictions on the transfer of shares, if any;
(c) The right of one or more shareholders to liquidate the company upon the occurrence of a specific or contingent event or voluntarily;
(d) Division or exercise of voting rights;
(e) Terms of appointment of officers, employees and workers of the company;
(f) Who shall be the director, officer or person bearing ultimate responsibility or chief executive of the company;
(g) Method of payment or distribution of dividends;

