**English Translation:**

165. Functions, duties and powers of Audit Committee: The functions, duties and powers of the audit committee constituted pursuant to sub-section (1) of Section 164 shall be as follows:
(a) To review the accounts and financial statements of the company and ascertain the truthfulness of the facts mentioned in such statements;
(b) To review the internal financial control system and risk management system of the company;
(c) To supervise and review the internal audit work of the company;
(d) To recommend the names of potential auditors for the appointment of the company's auditor, determine their remuneration and terms of appointment, and submit them to the general meeting for approval;
(e) To oversee and review whether the auditor of the company has complied with the code of conduct, standards and directives determined by the competent authority under the prevailing law while performing audit work;

दफा १६५: लेखापरीक्षण समितिको काम, कर्तव्य र अधिकार (Functions, duties and powers of Audit Committee)
d review whether the auditor of the company has complied with the code of conduct, standards and directives determined by the competent authority under the prevailing law while performing audit work;
(f) To determine the policy to be adopted by the company regarding the appointment and selection of the auditor based on the code of conduct, standards and directives prepared by the competent authority under the prevailing law;
(g) To prepare and implement or cause to be implemented the accounting policy of the company;
(h) If any regulatory body has made a provision for a long-form audit report to be disclosed in the company's audit report, to fulfill the necessary conditions to prepare such report;
(i) To perform other functions assigned by the board of directors in relation to the accounts, financial management and audit of the company.

