**English Translation:**

186. Functions, duties and powers of company secretary: (1) It shall be the duty of the company secretary to implement or cause to be implemented the decisions made by the board of directors and the general meeting and the matters directed by the Office or concerned bodies, and to submit the details, documents, decisions, etc., required to be submitted by the company to the Office or any other body under this Act or the prevailing law within the prescribed period.
(2) Subject to this Act, the memorandum of association and the articles of association, the company secretary shall perform the following functions:
(a) To call meetings of the board of directors or general meetings;
(b) To prepare the agenda of matters to be discussed in the meeting of the board of directors or general meeting and send it to the concerned directors or shareholders;
(c) To maintain records of the decisions of the meeting of the board of directors or general meeting, certify them and take charge of them;

दफा १८६: कम्पनी सचिवको काम, कर्तव्य र अधिकार (Functions, duties and powers of company secretary)
ing and send it to the concerned directors or shareholders;
(c) To maintain records of the decisions of the meeting of the board of directors or general meeting, certify them and take charge of them;
(d) To send notices of allotment of shares and calls for installments as per the decision of the board of directors;
(e) To maintain the register of shareholders and the records of shareholders and debenture-holders accurately, take charge of them and certify them;
(f) To submit matters relating to the pledge, transfer or registration of shares or debentures to the board of directors or the chief executive;
(g) If any claim, complaint, grievance, suggestion, advice, etc., is submitted in writing by a shareholder or debenture-holder, to forward it to the board of directors or the chief executive or the Office or other bodies, and to provide the result of the action taken in that regard in writing to the concerned shareholder or debenture-holder;
(h) To perform other functions determined or prescribed to be performed by the company secretary under the prevailing law.

दफा १८८: कम्पनी अध्यादेश, २०६२ निष्क्रिय भएपछि त्यसको परिणाम (Consequences of the Companies Ordinance, 2062 becoming inoperative)
ा सम्बन्धमा गररएको कुनै काम कारबाही िा उपायलाई असर पाने छैन र सो अध् यादेश कायम रहेसरह त् यस्िो कुनै कानूनी कारबाही िा उपायलाई पमन शुरु गनन, चालू राख्न िा लागू गनन सहकनेछ ।

**English Translation:**

188. Consequences of the Companies Ordinance, 2062 becoming inoperative: After the Companies Ordinance, 2062 (2005) becomes inoperative, unless a different intention appears, such inoperativeness shall not:
(a) Revive anything not in force or existing at the time at which the Ordinance becomes inoperative;
(b) Affect the previous operation of the Ordinance or anything duly done or suffered thereunder;
(c) Affect any right, privilege, obligation or liability acquired, accrued or incurred under the Ordinance;
(d) Affect any penalty, punishment or forfeiture incurred under the Ordinance;
(e) Affect any investigation, legal proceeding or remedy in respect of any such right, privilege, obligation, liability, penalty, punishment or forfeiture as aforesaid, and any such investigation, legal proceeding or remedy may be instituted, continued or enforced as if the Ordinance had not become inoperative.

